-- Rifts World Book 4: Africa - its named NPCs: 29 rows for `notable_npcs`,
-- their printed attacks in `stat_attacks` (owner_kind 'notable_npc'), and one
-- gear row for the body parts of Osiris.
--
--   the Four Horsemen (printed 12-35): Death, Famine, Pestilence, War, the
--     Armageddon Creature, and their mounts Bones, Cyno, Raid and Carnage
--   the Gods of Darkness (38-48): Set, Anubis, Apepi, Amon, Anhur, Ammit, Bes
--   the Gods of Light (49-59): Ra, Thoth, Isis, Horus, Bennu, Apis
--   the Phoenix Empire and the Gathering of Heroes (141-156): Pharaoh
--     Rama-Set, Katrina Sun (Isis in disguise, her own row by Nate's choice),
--     Victor Lazlo, Lo Fung, Fang-Lo, Abkii, and Sebek
--
-- NAMED TO SORT AFTER add-notable-npcs-dragons-and-gods.sql, whose fifteen rows
-- the last read-back checks; as add-africa-... it sorted first and found none.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-notable-npcs-rifts-africa.sql
--
-- THE THIRTEEN GODS TAKE `-africa` SLUGS. Palladium Fantasy Dragons and Gods
-- owns `set`, `ra`, `sebek` and the rest, in S.D.C.; this book restates them
-- for Rifts in M.D.C. with different levels and gear, the `hel` / `hel-norse`
-- precedent. The read-back asserts the fifteen Dragons and Gods rows are
-- untouched.
--
-- LEFT OUT: Erin Tarn and Sir Winslow Thorpe (printed 147-150), which Coalition
-- War Campaign, the later book, owns; Osiris, who has no stat block (his body
-- parts are the gear row below); and names printed with no stat block -
-- Lyphan the White Sphinx, Kryanthal, Tygre-Slnn, Rama-Set's advisors Hass
-- Uyban and Mbau Ngbuto.
--
-- EXTRACTED by four slices, every number read off a 170-200 dpi render; the
-- text layer here reads 5000 as SOOO and 1D6 as 106. Each named weapon rides
-- its owner's row. Judgement calls, each on its page: a Chiang-Ku dragon's
-- M.D.C. is its human form, the true form in bonuses_note; a god with two
-- classes carries the higher level and the full string in occ; Thoth's M.D.C.
-- is the actual 40,000, not the 14,470 he believes; Carnage's 2500 includes
-- its 1000 M.D.C. of armor; Rama-Set's real name is the printed Tor Li (also
-- known as Lo Li); Bes's restrained punch prints as M.D. and is kept, noted.
--
-- description and every prose field are paraphrases, checked for any
-- eight-word run shared with the book's text (stat lines and name lists aside).

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'death-horseman', 'Death', NULL, 'Leader of the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse', 'rifts', 'Horseman of the Apocalypse', '18th level Necromancer and Line Walker (equivalent)', 18, 'Diabolic', NULL, '12 feet (3.6 m), 13 feet (3.9 m) with his crown of horns', NULL, '{"IQ":21,"ME":27,"MA":27,"PS":42,"PP":20,"PE":30,"PB":4,"Spd":50}', NULL, NULL, 16633, 5000, 500, NULL, 19, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":6,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":6,"roll":2,"pull":6}', 'Four attacks per melee at minimum, plus one for each extra arm, tentacle or tail; strike and parry are +1 per arm, tentacle or tail (minimum +4, maximum +12). Critical strike on a natural 17-20. +6 save vs psionics, +6 save vs magic, +12 save vs horror factor; impervious to mind control, poison, drugs and magic potions. 92% to intimidate. Supernatural attributes; Spd 50 is about 35 mph (56 km). Magic fire, magic weapons and silver do double damage; Millennium Tree weapons do ten times damage. Each time one of the other three Horsemen dies, Death loses a quarter of his M.D.C., P.P.E., I.S.P. and level (round down).', '[{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Forensics","pct":98},{"name":"Pathology","pct":98},{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Skin & Prepare Animal Hides","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Track Animals","pct":98},{"name":"Track Humans","pct":80},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":80},{"name":"Prowl","pct":80},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":80}]', 'Has few other skills: no weapon proficiencies, no hand to hand skill, no piloting, reading or science.', 'Four arms and two legs, with nightvision 1200 feet (366 m), sees the invisible, and immunity to poison, drugs, gases and normal fire. Regenerates 1D4x1000 M.D.C. per minute and regrows a limb overnight. Powers over the dead: (1) grafts limbs from corpses onto himself in about 4 seconds each (arms 100 M.D.C., legs 150, wings/tails/tentacles 75); each extra arm or tentacle adds an attack and +1 strike/parry, legs add 10 Spd, wings give flight at Spd 35 up to 1000 feet; up to eight extra arms (12 total) and four extra legs (6 total). (2) Nightmare Zombies: stitches corpses into monsters in about 20 minutes (six to ten hours for large ones); he may create any number but controls at most 100; released ones hunt all life and fall apart after 60 days once more than 100 miles from him. Zombie stats: P.S. 24, P.P. 20, P.E. 20, P.B. 6, Spd 14, 1D4x100 M.D.C. (1D6x100 for elephant-sized or larger), Horror Factor 14 (16 giants), two attacks plus one per two extra limbs, +4 strike/parry/dodge (+6, and +10 P.S. and Spd, for giants), double damage from silver and magic. (3) Animates and controls 1D4x100 dead besides his zombies. (4) Decay touch: a one-month curse that rots the skin, halves P.B., M.A., combat bonuses and Spd, -15% skills, bars armor and heavy clothing, and nauseates everyone within 20 feet (-1 attack, -3 initiative). (5) Rigor mortis touch: a one-month curse halving attacks, combat bonuses and skills, Spd -75%, no initiative. Both touches need a 15 or better to save vs magic, cost one melee action each, and cannot pass sealed environmental armor, power armor or vehicles. (6) Stench of death: aura of fear, Horror Factor 19. Dog Boys and Psi-Stalkers sense him from a mile away (+20% to track). He will only kill those who attack him.', 'All necromancy and all spell magic, as an 18th level spell caster.', 'All healing and sensitive powers plus empathic transmission, mind bolt, mind bond, P.P.E. shield and psi-sword; 18th level Mind Melter equivalent, I.S.P. 500.', NULL, 'None; they do not function in him.', 'Staff of Death, a Greatest Rune Weapon: petrified bone staff with bat wings and a hovering horned skull; I.Q. 13, telepathic link to Death, indestructible, Diabolic (good beings touching it take 1D8 S.D.C. or 3D6 M.D.), +1 to all saves, soul drinker. 6D6 M.D. in melee, double to vampires and other undead. The skull fires lightning from its eyes for 1D6x10 M.D. at 2000 feet (610 m), one blast per user attack. Casts animate & control dead, turn dead, sickness, spoil, fear and shadow meld three times each per day at 10th level. Flies and fights on its own (three attacks, +3 strike/parry/dodge, +1 initiative); teleports back to Death on command and vanishes if he is destroyed. Devil Skulls: three horned skulls on his saddle that become 18 foot (5.5 m) winged skeleton warriors (400 M.D.C. each, Horror Factor 14, four attacks, +1 initiative, +6 strike, +7 parry/dodge, Spd 22 running or 58 flying, P.S. 24). Will also swing a corpse or a plucked limb as a club.', 'Neither needs nor wants any.', 'Cold, calm and calculating; moves with slow grace but can strike fast. Will not kill anyone who has not attacked him first, so he taunts and menaces victims until they lash out, then crushes them. Acts as the general of the other three, directing rather than fighting.', 'The other Horsemen and his netherbeast Bones; welcomes death worshippers such as Pharaoh Rama-Set and will make uneasy pacts with gods of death or darkness.', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'The skeletal, horned leader and brains of the Four Horsemen, a 12 foot tall figure of grey-purple rotting flesh with yellow-orange eyes. If the other three Horsemen are slain he fades from Earth unless a strong death cult anchors him, which is why he should never be attacked first.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.12-18');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'bones-netherbeast', 'Bones', NULL, 'Death''s steed', 'rifts', 'Netherbeast', 'Predatory riding beast', NULL, 'Miscreant (predatory animal)', NULL, '14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder; 30 feet (9.1 m) long', 'Eight tons', '{"ME":20,"MA":7,"PS":41,"PP":20,"PE":20,"PB":6,"Spd":77}', NULL, NULL, 1200, 50, NULL, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":4,"strike":8,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Bonuses include all bonuses. Critical strike on a natural 19-20. +3 save vs psionics, +3 save vs magic, +3 save vs poison and drugs. Typical netherbeasts have 4D4x100 M.D.C. and 1D6x10 P.P.E.; Bones has 1200 and 50. I.Q. is animal, roughly 7. Spd 77 is about 53 mph (85 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Animal I.Q. about 7, predatory. 14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder, 30 feet (9.1 m) long, eight tons. Can run at top speed for up to eight hours. Understands telepathic commands from its master. Eats flesh, blood and bone, living or dead.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Saddle of bone and leather; hung with chains, skulls, skeletons and corpses that Death can animate to bite or grab anyone close, or cut loose to fight, and can make the skulls seem to talk (tongues and ventriloquism).', NULL, 'A cunning, savage predator loyal to Death.', 'Death', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'Death''s mount, a huge beast like a cross between a pit bull and a dinosaur, pale with red eyes and ivory horns, draped with the dead.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.18-19');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'famine-horseman', 'Famine', NULL, 'Horseman of the Apocalypse, bringer of hunger', 'rifts', 'Horseman of the Apocalypse', '12th level Line Walker (equivalent)', 12, 'Diabolic', NULL, '10 feet (3 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":13,"ME":25,"MA":26,"PS":32,"PP":20,"PE":25,"PB":5,"Spd":77}', NULL, NULL, 6753, 2500, 250, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":4,"strike":5,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'Five hand to hand or psionic attacks, or two spells, per melee. Critical strike on a natural 19-20. +5 save vs psionics, +5 save vs magic, +10 save vs horror factor; immune to mind control, poison, drugs, and herbal or magic potions. 80% to intimidate. Supernatural attributes; Spd 77 is about 53 mph (85 km). Magic fire, magic weapons and silver do double damage; Millennium Tree weapons do ten times damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Botany","pct":98},{"name":"Skin & Prepare Animal Hides","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Track Animals","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Track Humanoids","pct":60},{"name":"Prowl","pct":60},{"name":"Pilot Sail and Row Boats","pct":60}]', 'No weapon proficiencies, hand to hand skill, reading or other science.', 'Never tires or sleeps; bio-regenerates 1D4x100 M.D.C. per minute and regrows a limb overnight; nightvision 1200 feet (366 m); sees the invisible; recognizes poisons and spoiled or diseased food; impervious to hunger, poison, drugs, gases, magic herbs and potions. Special powers (no P.P.E. unless noted): (1) Putrefy touch: each touch rots up to 2000 lb of food or 1000 gallons of water (one action); eaters must save vs non-lethal poison (16+) or for 24 hours lose initiative and two attacks, -2 combat, -10% skills, half Spd. (2) Starvation touch: victim must save vs magic at 14+ or spend an hour ravenously seeking food, able to defend but not attack, then vomits and is -1 to combat for 1D4 hours; reaches a victim in environmental body armor, though power armor, robots and sealed vehicles block it. (3) Aura of hunger, 200 foot (60 m) radius: -1 initiative and -5% skills, worsening after ten minutes to -3 initiative, -1 combat, -15% skills and -10% Spd. (4) Water divining: 50 P.P.E., finds water within 100 miles (160 km) for four hours. (5) Limited weather control: 1200 P.P.E., two mile (3.2 km) radius for 3D4 days; heat wave, drought, frost, hail or high winds, and can combine two.', 'All line walker spells of levels 1-7 plus eyes of the wolf, negate magic, oracle, spoil, stone to flesh, mute, protection circles (simple and superior), calm storms, summon rain, summon storm, close rift, dimensional portal and teleport: superior; 12th level spell caster.', 'All physical powers plus telepathy, bio-manipulation, group mind block, hydrokinesis, pyrokinesis, P.P.E. shield and telekinesis (super); 12th level Mind Melter equivalent, I.S.P. 250.', NULL, 'None; they do not function in him.', 'Staff of Decay, a Greatest Rune Weapon: petrified wood staff topped with dead leaves and a skull, reeking of rot and trailed by flies; I.Q. 10, telepathic link to Famine, indestructible, reddish grey, Diabolic (good beings touching it take 1D8 S.D.C. or 3D6 M.D.), +1 to all saves, soul drinker. 6D6 M.D. in melee, double to vampires and other undead, 3D4x10 M.D. to Millennium Trees. The skull fires blue energy bolts for 1D4x10 M.D. (triple to Millennium Trees) at 2000 feet (610 m), one per user attack. Casts, three times each per day: wind rush, wisps of confusion, call lightning, turn dead, spoil and invisibility: superior three times each per day at 8th level. Returns to him by teleport and leaves Earth if he is destroyed.', 'Neither needs nor wants any.', 'Sly, treacherous and patient; prefers to strike from hiding or afar and to disguise his work as natural disaster, and loves setting starving communities against each other.', 'The other Horsemen, Pestilence above all, and his netherbeast Cyno; welcomes death worshippers such as Pharaoh Rama-Set and uneasy pacts with dark gods.', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'A 10 foot tall withered, skeletal horseman with swept-back ram''s horns, pinkish white skin and pale blue glowing eyes. He spreads starvation by spoiling food and water and by twisting the weather against crops.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.19-23');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'cyno-netherbeast', 'Cyno', NULL, 'Famine''s steed', 'rifts', 'Netherbeast', 'Predatory riding beast', NULL, 'Miscreant (predatory animal)', NULL, '14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder; 30 feet (9.1 m) long', 'Eight tons', '{"ME":20,"MA":7,"PS":43,"PP":22,"PE":22,"PB":4,"Spd":77}', NULL, NULL, 1000, 50, NULL, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":4,"strike":9,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Bonuses include all bonuses. Critical strike on a natural 19-20. +3 save vs psionics, +4 save vs magic, +4 save vs poison and drugs. Typical netherbeasts have 4D4x100 M.D.C. and 1D6x10 P.P.E. I.Q. is animal, about 7. Spd 77 is about 53 mph (85 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Animal I.Q. about 7, predatory. 14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder, 30 feet (9.1 m) long, eight tons. Can run at top speed for up to eight hours. Understands telepathic commands from its master. Very fast and agile; feeds on meat, blood and bone, and on rotting food and plants too.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Plain riding harness, reins and leather saddle.', NULL, 'A cunning predator loyal to Famine.', 'Famine', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'Famine''s gaunt, white or pale grey netherbeast with horns swept back over its head, red eyes and grey, decayed-looking teeth and horns.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.23');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'pestilence-horseman', 'Pestilence', NULL, 'Horseman of the Apocalypse, lord of plague and swarm', 'rifts', 'Horseman of the Apocalypse', '10th level Line Walker (equivalent)', 10, 'Diabolic', NULL, '10 feet (3 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":16,"ME":24,"MA":24,"PS":39,"PP":22,"PE":30,"PB":4,"Spd":88}', NULL, NULL, 7123, 1500, 250, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":8,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Six hand to hand, insect or psionic attacks, or two spells, per melee. Critical strike on a natural 19-20. +5 save vs psionics, +8 save vs magic, +8 save vs poisons and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor; impervious to mind control, insect poisons and disease. 70% to intimidate. Supernatural attributes; Spd 88 is about 60 mph (96 km). Magic fire, magic weapons and silver do double damage; Millennium Tree weapons do ten times damage. The bugs that make up his body can be hurt by fire, heat, insecticides and gases, and cold sends them dormant.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Chemistry","pct":98},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":98},{"name":"Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Track Animals","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Climb","pct":60},{"name":"Swim","pct":60},{"name":"Track Humanoids","pct":60}]', 'No weapon proficiencies, hand to hand skill, reading or other science.', 'A horned bone skeleton whose flesh is a living mass of insects and arachnids by the tens of thousands; controls them and up to 500,000 other bugs at once. Bio-regenerates 100 points per minute and regrows a limb overnight; nightvision 1200 feet (366 m); sees the invisible; identifies insects, disease and poisons and spoiled food; impervious to hunger, insect bites and poisons, and most diseases. Special powers: (1) Body of bugs: anyone touching him is swarmed, taking 4D6 S.D.C. per round unless armored, with half attacks and half combat bonuses for eight rounds (or two rounds spent doing nothing but brushing them off at 2D6); even armored foes are -1. (2) Engulf: pulls a victim into his body for 3D4x10 S.D.C. per round, a disease roll and a save vs insanity (17+) against a trauma table of phobias and obsessions. (3) Swarms released from his body for ten minutes or longer: blinding cloud (visibility six feet, half actions, no initiative or combat bonuses, Spd -70%), biting swarm (3D4x10 S.D.C. per round), deadly swarm of 4D6x10 spiders and scorpions (3D6 S.D.C. per sting, three to twelve stings per round), devouring swarm that strips crops, and a disease-carrying swarm. Diseases: pox, fever, sickness, plague and a terrible cold, each with heavy penalties for days (save vs non-lethal poison 16+ halves). (4) Disease touch: inflicts one of those diseases for one action and 100 P.P.E. (5) Infests food or carcasses with maggots and vermin at no cost. (6) Senses sickness and contamination.', 'All line walker spells of levels 1-5 plus apparition, hallucination, tongues, negate magic, sickness, spoil, mute, protection circles (simple and superior), summon & control insects (1D6x1000 insects, 5 hours per level, 125 P.P.E.), summon & control rodents, close rift, dimensional portal, and all curses and insanities; 10th level spell caster.', 'All healing powers plus presence sense, empathy, telepathy, bio-manipulation, group mind block, pyrokinesis, P.P.E. shield, telekinesis (super) and telekinetic force field; 10th level Mind Melter equivalent, I.S.P. 250.', NULL, 'None; they do not function in him.', 'Staff of Destruction, a Greatest Rune Weapon: tapered black metal rod crowned by a death''s-head beetle; I.Q. 10, telepathic link to Pestilence, indestructible, Diabolic (good beings touching it take 1D8 S.D.C. or 3D6 M.D.), +1 to all saves. 1D4x10 M.D. in melee, double to vampires and other undead, 3D4x10 M.D. to Millennium Trees. Its hive fires an energy bolt for 1D6x10 M.D. (triple to Millennium Trees) at 2000 feet (610 m), one per user attack, and releases six magic beetles that grow to five feet long (120 M.D.C. each, three attacks, 3D6 M.D. bite, +3 strike/parry, +6 dodge, fly at Spd 154), regrown in 24 hours if destroyed. Returns to him by teleport and leaves Earth if he is destroyed.', 'Neither needs nor wants any.', 'Clever and resourceful, mixing trickery with open attack; takes special pleasure in slow death by disease and hunger, and would destroy even the insects he commands.', 'The other Horsemen, Famine above all, and his giant beetle Raid; welcomes death worshippers such as Pharaoh Rama-Set and uneasy pacts with dark gods.', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'From afar a burly horned humanoid, up close a 10 foot bone skeleton wrapped in a seething, shifting coat of insects, with green glowing eyes. He unleashes swarms and plagues on everything living.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.23-27');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'raid-netherbeast', 'Raid', NULL, 'Pestilence''s steed', 'rifts', 'Netherbeast', 'Giant flying beetle (riding beast)', NULL, 'Miscreant (predatory insect)', NULL, '14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder; 30 feet (9.1 m) long', 'Eight tons', '{"ME":10,"MA":10,"PS":44,"PP":22,"PE":24,"PB":5,"Spd":77}', NULL, NULL, 1500, 10, NULL, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":7,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"roll":3}', 'Bonuses include all bonuses. Critical strike on a natural 19-20. +3 save vs psionics, +5 save vs magic, +5 save vs poison and drugs. Typical of its kind: 4D4x100+100 M.D.C., 2D6 P.P.E. Low animal I.Q. about 3. Spd 77 (53 mph) running, 132 (90 mph/148 km) flying.', NULL, NULL, 'A giant armored beetle with a single horn and huge mandibles; quick, agile and able to fly for 1D4+1 hours before resting. Feeds on meat, blood and bone, and on rotting food and plants too. Understands telepathic commands from its master.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A predatory insect loyal to Pestilence.', 'Pestilence', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'Pestilence rides this giant red-brown beetle with black markings, yellow eyes and belly and red mandibles, rather than a true netherbeast.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.27-29');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'war-horseman', 'War', NULL, 'Horseman of the Apocalypse, the weapon master', 'rifts', 'Horseman of the Apocalypse', '10th level Warrior and Line Walker (equivalent)', 10, 'Diabolic', NULL, 'Typically 12 feet; can change from 6 to 24 feet', NULL, '{"IQ":16,"ME":26,"MA":26,"PS":56,"PP":26,"PE":26,"PB":6,"Spd":86}', NULL, NULL, 8482, 2000, 350, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":10,"initiative":6,"strike":8,"parry":8,"dodge":10,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Ten hand to hand or psionic attacks, or two spells, per melee. Strike +8 bare-handed, +11 with modern or energy weapons, +13 with ancient weapons such as ball and chain; parry +8 bare-handed, +12 with any weapon. Critical strike on a natural 17-20. +6 save vs psionics, magic, and poisons and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor; impervious to mind control, fatigue and disease. 80% to stir intimidation, hate, anger and vengeance with his words. Supernatural attributes; Spd 86 is about 59 mph (94 km). Magic fire, magic weapons and silver do double damage; Millennium Tree weapons do ten times damage; ordinary M.D. weapons do normal damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Scrambler","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Laser","pct":98},{"name":"T.V./Video","pct":98},{"name":"Operate Computer","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Programming","pct":98},{"name":"Automotive Mechanics","pct":98},{"name":"Robot Mechanics","pct":98},{"name":"Mechanical Engineer","pct":98},{"name":"Weapons Engineer","pct":98},{"name":"Weapon Systems","pct":98},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":98},{"name":"Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Basic Electronics","pct":98},{"name":"Climb","pct":75},{"name":"Swim","pct":75},{"name":"Track Humanoids","pct":75},{"name":"Track Animals","pct":75},{"name":"Pilot Tanks & APCs","pct":75},{"name":"Pilot Combat Helicopters","pct":75},{"name":"Pilot Jet Fighters","pct":75},{"name":"Pilot Combat Robots","pct":75}]', 'Uses any weapon as an expert. At 75% can pilot every combat vehicle. No medicine, science or book learning; communicates by magic and telepathy.', 'Expert with all weapons. His apparent armor is his body and bio-regenerates 1D6x100 M.D.C. per minute; regrows a limb in 6D6 minutes. Nightvision 1200 feet (366 m), sees the invisible, can judge any weapon and its quality, needs no food, water or rest, never falls ill, and highly resistant to drugs. Special powers: (1) Weapon Meld: merges with any weapon, vehicle or war machine (never ordinary machines, and never one already piloted), making it part of his body and using it with full expertise; can take over and reprogram an empty robot in one minute. (2) Power Meld: powers melded weapons and engines himself, giving energy weapons unlimited payload and turning projectile weapons into endless energy bolts; cannot create explosives or missiles but can arm and launch existing ones. (3) Changes size in one foot steps from 6 to 24 feet at will; his armor and magic weapons grow with him, his netherbeast does not. (4) Mechanical genius with telemechanics; repairs and modifies weapons and war machines. His words can whip mobs into violence.', 'All line walker spells of levels 1-4 plus tongues, words of truth, swim as a fish (superior), energy disruption, circle of flame, fire ball, negate magic, banishment, protection circles (simple and superior), id barrier, anti-magic cloud (which also blocks the Horsemen''s own spells), close rift and dimensional portal; 10th level spell caster.', 'All physical powers plus presence sense, sixth sense, telepathy, telemechanics, electrokinesis, pyrokinesis, mind bolt, psi-shield and psi-sword; 10th level Mind Melter equivalent, I.S.P. 350.', NULL, 'None; has no use for them.', 'Rune Ball & Chain, a Greatest Rune Weapon: flaming spiked ball whose fire cannot be put out; I.Q. 11, telepathic link to War, indestructible, red, Diabolic (good beings touching it take 1D8 S.D.C. or 3D6 M.D.), +1 to all saves, soul drinker. 1D6x10 M.D., double to vampires and other undead, 3D6x10 M.D. to Millennium Trees; chain stretches from 3 to 100 feet, returns when thrown (range 1000 feet/305 m), and can entangle and hold a foe on its own. Twin shoulder lasers: 4D6 M.D. single or 1D4x10+8 M.D. dual, 2000 feet (610 m), up to ten blasts per round, each using an attack. From his netherbeast: magic chains (150 M.D.C., 3D6 M.D. whip or bola, 70% trip, 200 feet thrown), smaller manacle chains (100 M.D.C., unpickable, proof against escape), throwing rings (2D6 M.D., 200 feet), plucked spikes (2D6 M.D., 100 feet), three magic skulls (2D6 M.D., 200 feet, or smoke over a 500 foot radius) and crossbones (5D6 M.D. boomerangs, 500 feet, return to him), and an arsenal of plain M.D. weapons: 1D4 morning stars or maces 2D6, 1D4 battle axes 3D6, 1D4 javelins 1D6, 2D4 spears 2D6, one runka pole arm 4D6. Others using his gear do half damage at half range.', 'Neither needs nor wants any.', 'The most aggressive and warlike Horseman: a merciless killer, brilliant strategist and dirty fighter who kills the helpless without a qualm and turns on any ally at the first sign of betrayal.', 'The other Horsemen and his netherbeast Carnage; welcomes death worshippers such as Pharaoh Rama-Set and uneasy pacts with dark gods.', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'A 12 foot warrior in blood red armor that is actually his own body, with a horned helm showing only darkness through its eye slit. The deadliest of the three Horsemen who must die to banish Death.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.30-33');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'carnage-netherbeast', 'Carnage', NULL, 'War''s steed', 'rifts', 'Netherbeast', 'Predatory riding beast', NULL, 'Diabolic (predatory animal)', NULL, '14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder; 30 feet (9.1 m) long', 'Eight tons', '{"ME":20,"MA":9,"PS":50,"PP":22,"PE":24,"PB":4,"Spd":110}', NULL, NULL, 2500, 50, NULL, NULL, 15, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":5,"strike":10,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"roll":6,"pull":4}', 'Bonuses include all bonuses. Critical strike on a natural 19-20. +3 save vs psionics, +5 save vs magic, +5 save vs poison, drugs and disease. M.D.C. is 1500 natural plus 1000 from its body armor; each plasma cannon has 150. I.Q. is animal, about 7. Spd 110 is about 75 mph (120 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Animal I.Q. about 7, predatory. 14 feet (4.3 m) at the shoulder, 30 feet (9.1 m) long, eight tons. Can run at top speed for up to eight hours. Understands telepathic commands from its master. The fastest and strongest of the netherbeasts; kills for pleasure and eats only fresh kills.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Metallic red M.D.C. body armor (1000 M.D.C.) and two long-range plasma cannons behind the shoulders (150 M.D.C. each), usable only while War rides or touches it: 1D6x10 M.D. single or 2D6x10 M.D. dual, 6000 feet (1828 m), up to ten blasts per round using War''s attacks, unlimited payload, 360 degree turret. Carries War''s chains, rings, spikes, skulls and crossbones, and his arsenal of ancient M.D. weapons.', NULL, 'As savage as its master; a pure killer.', 'War', 'Heroes who hunt the Horsemen one at a time before they can reunite; anyone who attacks them.', 'War''s grey, ram-horned netherbeast clad in red armor and bristling with weapons, the fastest and most aggressive of the Horsemen''s mounts.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.33-34');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'armageddon-creature', 'The Armageddon Creature', NULL, 'Four as One, a primordial force of destruction', 'rifts', 'Horseman of the Apocalypse (the four merged)', '20th level Warrior and Line Walker (equivalent)', 20, 'Diabolic', NULL, '60 feet (18 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":26,"ME":30,"MA":30,"PS":80,"PP":30,"PE":30,"PB":2,"Spd":293}', NULL, NULL, 36000, 20000, 5000, NULL, 19, '{"attacks":20,"initiative":10,"strike":10,"dodge":10,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Twenty hand to hand, psionic or special power attacks, or four spells, per melee. Strike +10 bare-handed, +11 with modern or energy weapons, +13 with ancient weapons; +12 using any weapon (the printed block lists no bare-hand parry). Critical strike on a natural 17-20; +10 on all saving throws. Supernatural attributes; Spd 293 is about 200 mph (321 km). Magic fire, magic weapons and silver do double damage; Millennium Tree weapons do ten times damage; ordinary M.D. weapons do normal damage. If only three Horsemen merge, size, attributes, P.P.E., I.S.P., level, damage and powers drop by 25%; with two, by 50%; one alone cannot become it, and a missing Horseman''s powers are lost.', NULL, 'All the skills of the four combined.', 'All natural and special powers of the four Horsemen, greatly amplified. Regenerates 1D4x1000 M.D.C. per minute and regrows limbs in 6D6 minutes. As an intangible force it spreads war, drought, disaster and plague worldwide, ending human and D-bee life within a decade; its physical form can raise armies of robots, fanatics and dead and cast disease and weather over 40,000 square miles at a time. The four merge only at a powerful ley line nexus when the planets align or the sun is eclipsed, or through a magic pyramid on a nexus, ideally with a fifth party (Rama-Set) directing the energy.', 'All magic of the four.', 'All psionics of the four.', NULL, NULL, 'Wields War''s Rune Ball & Chain, its ball now a flaming skull, and the staves of Famine and Pestilence twisted into one.', NULL, 'Bent on destroying every living thing.', 'None.', 'All life.', 'The Four Horsemen fused into one 60 foot giant: an emaciated body with eight to twelve arms, grey and red armor like War''s, and Death''s head. Its coming would doom Rifts Earth within years.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.34-35');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'set-africa', 'Set', 'Set Typhon-Tanis', 'Lord of Darkness', 'rifts', 'Deity', '20th level Ley Line Walker and Shifter, 12th level Stone Master, Fire Warlock, Diabolist', 20, 'Diabolic', NULL, '25 feet (7.6 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":21,"ME":26,"MA":25,"PS":37,"PP":20,"PE":30,"PB":10,"Spd":27}', NULL, NULL, 16850, 6000, 2950, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":4,"strike":5,"parry":10,"dodge":10,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'Seven hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 19-20, triple damage from behind. +6 save vs psionics, +10 save vs all magic, +8 save vs poison and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor; 85% to evoke intimidation, fear or trust. Supernatural P.S. and attributes. Spd 27 is about 18.5 mph. Holy weapons, silver weapons (which do M.D. to him), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do double damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Anthropology","pct":98},{"name":"Biology","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Disguise","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Sail and Row Boats","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":65},{"name":"Climbing","pct":65},{"name":"Swimming","pct":65},{"name":"Forgery","pct":65},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":65},{"name":"Tracking (humanoids)","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":65}]', 'W.P. Blunt and W.P. Sword (listed among the 65% skills; no percentage applies).', 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 98%, dimensional teleport 92%, metamorphosis into any shape at will, immune to fire, cold and heat. Summons 1000-6000 rats, mice or bats, and can summon and command 1D4 jinn or 2D4 worms of Taut (any). Priestly powers: exorcism 80%, turn dead 90% (2D6x100 dead at once), animate/control 1D6x100 dead 97%, healing touch 3D6 S.D.C./hit points twice per melee (each uses an action), bio-regeneration 1D6x100 M.D.C./minute (new limb overnight). Resurrection touch: one attempt per subject; dead no more than a month succeeds on 01-70% (revived with full S.D.C. and 3D6 hit points, the fatal injury healed but not lost limbs or scars); dead a month to a year 01-32%; over a year 2%.', 'All spell magic levels 1-7, all stone magic, fire elemental magic levels 1-8, every symbol, curse and ward, protection and summoning circles, and additionally close rift, dimensional portal, remove curse, stone to flesh and teleport: superior. Ley line magic at 20th level; stone, elemental and ward/diabolist magic at 12th level. Saving throw vs his spells is 16 or higher.', 'I.S.P. 2950 at 20th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: all level 1-5 powers. Rifts: all physical and sensitive powers plus pyrokinesis and mind block auto-defense.', NULL, NULL, 'Black Rod of the Four Winds: greatest rune staff topped with an ankh, his badge of office; I.Q. 15, telepathic link, indestructible, reddish grey, diabolic (1D6x10 damage per melee to a good being holding it); 3D4x10 M.D.; casts summon storm, call lightning, fear, wind rush, extinguish fires and supernatural darkness (1000 ft/305 m radius, horror factor 10, normal vision blinded and enhanced vision cut to 25% range, lasts up to 8 hours) six times each per 24 hours at 15th level; teleports back to Set on command, even across dimensions. The Impaler: rune sword (Rifts Atlantis p.130); I.Q. 9, telepathic link, indestructible, black, diabolic (6D6 S.D.C. or M.D. per melee to a good being holding it), soul drinker; 1D6x10 M.D. in melee; four spiked finger appendages shoot out twice per melee for 2D4+2 M.D. each or 1D4x10 M.D. with all four on one target, +2 to strike; can animate and scuttle like a spider (Spd 12, climb 80%, two attacks or four other actions per melee). Armor: chain and plate in black and silver, 3000 M.D.C. Shuns bionics and cybernetics; has access to Atlantean bio-wizardry.', '2D4 billion credits in precious metals and gems, plus assorted magic and technological items.', 'A crafty master strategist and silver-tongued tempter who goads others toward cruelty, murder and revenge by playing on their anger and grief; highly social and political.', 'Closest to Anubis (whom he treats as a son), Bes and Apepi; friends with Lord Splynncryth and two other Splugorth; ties to demon lords such as Mephisto, Modeus and the Four Demon Beetles; backs the Gargoyle Empire against Triax and the NGR; Pharaoh Rama-Set is his chief disciple; worshipped by most non-humans of the Phoenix Empire; new contacts in the Federation of Magic. Summons jinn and worms of Taut; uses elementals, gargoyles, tautons, hell hounds and dar''ota; favors raksasha, mindolar, baal-rog and gargoyle lords.', 'Gods of Light and humankind; murderer of his brother Osiris.', 'The Egyptian god of evil, deceit and fratricide, who slew Osiris and scattered his body in fourteen pieces. He appears as a giant with a hyena''s (or wolf''s) head and is usually attended by Bes or Apepi.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.38-40');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'anubis-africa', 'Anubis', 'Anupi', 'Lord of the Dead', 'rifts', 'Deity', '14th level Necromancer, 8th level Diabolist and Stone Master', 14, 'Aberrant', NULL, '20 feet (6 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":20,"ME":24,"MA":22,"PS":40,"PP":22,"PE":25,"PB":10,"Spd":44}', NULL, NULL, 12450, 3500, 1450, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":5,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'Six hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 19-20, triple damage from behind. +6 save vs psionics, +8 save vs all magic, +6 save vs poison and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor; 70% to evoke intimidation, fear or trust. Supernatural P.S.; Spd 44 is 30 mph. Holy weapons, silver weapons (which do M.D. to him), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do double damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Biology","pct":98},{"name":"Chemistry","pct":98},{"name":"Pathology","pct":98},{"name":"Forensics","pct":98},{"name":"Paramedic","pct":98},{"name":"Skin and Prepare Animal Hides","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Dance","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":60},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":60},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":60}]', 'W.P. Blunt, W.P. Sword and W.P. Energy Rifle, each equal to 6th level.', 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 96%, dimensional teleport 86%, metamorphosis into any shape, heat, cold and fire do half damage. Summons 1D6x100 rats, mice or bats and summons/commands 3D4 Alu demons. Priestly powers: exorcism 95%, turn dead 98% (4D6x100 dead), animate/control 2D6x100 dead 97%, healing touch 3D6 S.D.C./hit points once per melee, bio-regeneration 3D6x10 M.D.C./minute (new limb overnight).', 'Every necromancy spell and ability, common spell magic levels 1-6, all illusion magic, circles of protection and summoning, and also banishment, close rift, control/enslave entity, create mummy, create zombie, dimensional portal, exorcism, life drain and teleport: superior; basic diabolism and all stone magic. Necromancy at 14th level, diabolism and stone magic at 8th. Saving throw vs his magic is 15 or higher.', 'I.S.P. 1450 at 12th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: all level 1-5 powers. Rifts: all physical powers plus hydrokinesis, mind block auto-defense, mind bolt, object read, presence sense, psi-shield, psi-sword and telepathy.', NULL, NULL, 'Sword of Anubis: greatest rune sword; I.Q. 14, telepathic link, indestructible, grey, diabolic (1D4x10 damage per melee to a good being holding it); 2D4x10 M.D.; casts agony, blind, circle of flame, fire ball, mute and negate magic six times each per 24 hours at 10th level; drinks both souls and blood. Armor: chain and plate in blue, 2000 M.D.C. Shuns bionics and cybernetics; indifferent to suspicious about technology.', 'About a billion credits in precious metals and gems, plus assorted magic and technological items.', 'Cold, cunning and merciless toward opposition; utterly loyal to Set and content to be second. Arrogant, and prone to underestimating humans and other lesser beings.', 'Closest to Set and Bes; shares many of Set''s contacts on worse terms; best friends with Pharaoh Rama-Set and revered by the Phoenix Empire''s non-humans; urges Set''s aid to the Gargoyle Empire. Summons Alu demons; uses worms of Taut, hell hounds, magots, grave ghouls, banshees and nightmares; favors night owls, dimensional ghouls and death weaver spider demons. Ammit serves him.', 'Gods of Light; Lord Splynncryth dislikes him; Apepi dislikes him.', 'Son of Osiris and Nephthys who helped bring about his father''s murder, now Set''s right hand and a lord of necromancy with an army of mummies. He has a muscular man''s body and a jackal''s head and usually travels with 3D4 mummies, Set or Bes.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.40-42');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'apepi-africa', 'Apepi', 'Apepi Apophis', 'The Immortal, Dragon God', 'rifts', 'Dragon (unique species)', '8th level Spell Caster and Stone Master', 8, 'Diabolic', NULL, '30 feet (9 m) long, 12 feet (3.6 m) tall', NULL, '{"IQ":9,"ME":14,"MA":19,"PS":58,"PP":25,"PE":24,"PB":5,"Spd":44}', NULL, NULL, 6900, 1000, 480, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":6,"strike":8,"parry":10,"dodge":10,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Seven hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 18-20 and from behind. +3 save vs psionics, +6 save vs all magic, +6 save vs poison and drugs, +8 save vs horror factor; 55% to evoke intimidation or trust. Supernatural P.S.; Spd 44 is 30 mph, flies at Spd 66. Also called Apepi the Indestructible and the Immortal One. Vulnerable: holy weapons, silver (does M.D. to him), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do TRIPLE damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":65},{"name":"Climbing","pct":65},{"name":"Palming","pct":65},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":65}]', 'W.P. Blunt and W.P. Sword, each equal to 10th level.', 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 89%, dimensional teleport 31%, flies at Spd 66 (45 mph/72 km), heat, cold and fire do half damage. Exorcism 81%, turn dead 57% (1D6x10 dead). Bio-regenerates 2D4x100 M.D.C./minute, limbs regrown in 1D4x10 minutes. Immortal: reduced to zero or below he revives at full strength in 2D4 hours; if taken more than 300 below zero or vaporized, he returns at full power 48 hours later.', 'All warlock air spells, or all common air and water spells, plus all stone magic, all at 8th level. Saving throw vs his magic is 13 or higher.', 'I.S.P. 480 at 8th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: all level 1-5 powers. Rifts: all physical powers plus empathy, telepathy, presence sense, sixth sense, electrokinesis, hydrokinesis, telekinesis (super) and mind bolt.', NULL, NULL, 'No special magic weapons, no favorite weapons and no armor; fights with strength, claws, magic and psionics. Refuses all technology and attacks high-tech targets first.', 'A modest hoard worth roughly 200 million credits, kept to bait the greedy and pay for spies and assassins.', 'Insane, sadistic and reckless, courting death because he cannot stay dead; relishes pain and remembers everyone who ever killed him. Obeys Set to the letter; only Set restrains his bloodlust.', 'Bound to Set by a pact of eternal service in exchange for an immortality potion; counts Bes and Thoth as friends; likes Pharaoh Rama-Set; favors tautons and worms of Taut and commands whatever minions Set assigns.', 'Ra above all, who has killed him many times; all Gods of Light and good beings; Set''s foes; dislikes Anubis; wielders of technology.', 'A one-of-a-kind winged serpent dragon with two clawed arms and a slashing tail, made immortal and mad by a legendary potion Set gave him. Should Set ever die, Apepi will be loosed on the Megaverse on an endless killing spree.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.42-43');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'amon-africa', 'Amon', 'Ammon-Ra', 'The Hidden One', 'rifts', 'Deity', '11th level Fire Warlock, 11th level Diabolist, 11th level Stone Master', 11, 'Aberrant', NULL, '19 feet (5.9 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":19,"ME":11,"MA":20,"PS":30,"PP":23,"PE":25,"PB":2,"Spd":44}', NULL, NULL, 10473, 1600, 1250, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":4,"strike":5,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"roll":3,"pull":5}', 'Up to seven attacks per melee: six hand to hand or psionic plus one fire vomit, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 19-20, triple damage from behind. +6 save vs psionics, +8 save vs all magic, +6 save vs poison and drugs, +11 save vs horror factor; 60% to evoke intimidation, fear or trust. Supernatural P.S.; runs at Spd 44 (30 mph), flies at Spd 88. Holy weapons, silver weapons (which do M.D. to her), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do double damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Dance","pct":98},{"name":"Sing","pct":98},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Flute","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":60},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":60},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":60}]', 'W.P. Energy Rifle, Knife, Pistol and Sword, each equal to 6th level. Her flute tunes are macabre.', 'Flies at Spd 88 (60 mph/96 km), nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 91%, dimensional teleport 47%, impervious to heat and fire, summons 1D6x100 rats, mice or bats. Spews mega-damage fire once per melee (an extra attack): 1D4x10 M.D., range 100 ft (30.5 m). Priestly powers: exorcism 86%, turn dead 92% (1D4x100 dead), animate/control 4D4 dead 92%, healing touch 3D6 S.D.C./hit points once per melee, resurrection 44%, bio-regeneration 1D4x100 M.D.C./minute (new limb overnight).', 'All warlock fire spells, or all common fire and related spells, plus all stone magic, all at 11th level. Saving throw vs her magic is 14 or higher.', 'I.S.P. 1250 at 11th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: all level 1-5 powers. Rifts: all sensitive powers plus bio-manipulation, empathic transmission, hypnotic suggestion and pyrokinesis.', NULL, NULL, 'Blood Fellow: lesser rune dagger used for torture, always at her side; I.Q. 16, telepathic link, indestructible, dark red, diabolic (1D8 S.D.C., 3D6 M.D. against M.D.C. beings, per melee to a good being holding it); damage adjustable in 1D6 steps up to 5D6 M.D., or S.D.C. in the same steps against S.D.C. victims; drinks souls and blood. The Enslaver: rune device shaped like a stylized insect statue with the eight standard rune weapon abilities (Rifts Atlantis p.127); casts compulsion, dominance, fear, mask of deceit and trance three times each per 24 hours; psionics with 2D6x10+100 I.S.P.: psi-sword (up to 8D6 M.D.), psi-shield (80 M.D.C.), bio-manipulation, empathy, hypnotic suggestion, empathic transmission, mentally possess others, mind block auto-defense, mind bolt, mind bond, mind wipe, see the invisible, sense evil, sense magic, sixth sense and telepathy. Also a psi-interrogator, ten Eylor seeker-hunter eyes, and at her lair 3D4 each of chest amalgamates, transfortifiers, brain feeders, mystic leeches and zombitrons. No armor. Loathes and destroys all technology.', '6D6x10 million credits in precious metals and gems, though she cares little for wealth.', 'Maddened and bitter over her disfigurement, she hides among the dead and monstrous and delights in maiming beautiful beings and leaving them alive to suffer as she does.', 'Favors Anhur among the gods; counts Lord Splynncryth among her rare friends; he trades her bio-wizard organisms for information; commands an army of deformed minions of her own making; uses elementals, boschala, tectonic entities, malignous, gorgons and tautons; sometimes works with goquas and death weaver spider demons.', 'Thoth, who disfigured her, and the Gods of Light; resents Set and Anubis, whom she blames, though she has never struck at them; all attractive beings, especially angels, titans, elves and dragons; technology users.', 'Once the loveliest of the Gods of Light, she betrayed Osiris to Set out of wounded pride and was permanently disfigured by Thoth''s magic in the war that followed. She now appears as a hag with a melted-wax face and boil-covered skin, and is popular among ugly non-humans.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.43-44');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'anhur-africa', 'Anhur', 'Anher Thinis', 'The Slayer of Enemies', 'rifts', 'Deity', '15th level Headhunter (warrior), 10th level Ley Line Walker, 5th level Diabolist and Stone Master', 15, 'Aberrant', NULL, '18 feet (5.5 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":22,"ME":24,"MA":24,"PS":51,"PP":28,"PE":30,"PB":20,"Spd":88}', NULL, NULL, 7470, 1230, NULL, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":7,"strike":10,"parry":12,"dodge":12,"roll":7,"pull":7}', 'M.D.C. 7470 is before armor. Seven hand to hand attacks per melee or two by spell. +10 strike is hand to hand; +9 to strike with energy weapons. Critical strike on a natural 18-20. +6 save vs psionics, +9 save vs all magic, +9 save vs poison and drugs, +9 save vs horror factor; 80% to evoke intimidation or trust, 50% charm/impress. Supernatural P.S.; Spd 88 is 60 mph. Holy weapons, silver weapons (which do M.D. to him), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do double damage. Magic cold hurts him double as well.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Hover Vehicles","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Boats","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":65},{"name":"Radio: Scrambler","pct":65},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":65},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese","pct":65},{"name":"Literacy: Euro","pct":65}]', 'All W.P.s and all espionage skills at 98%.', 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 94%, dimensional teleport 53%, flies at 75 mph (120 km), never tires, rarely sleeps and is always alert, bio-regenerates 4D6x100 M.D.C./minute (new limb overnight). Priestly powers: exorcism 61%, turn dead 69% (3D6x10 dead), remove magic curse 64%, resurrection 33%, unlimited healing touch 3D6 S.D.C./hit points.', 'All stone magic and ley line walker spells levels 1-6, and also anti-magic cloud, close rift, dimensional portal, dispel magic barrier, metamorphosis: human, mystic portal, negate magic, protection circles, speed of the snail, teleport: superior and wards. Ley line magic at 10th level, stone magic and diabolism at 5th. Diabolism limited to symbols, rune reading and basic ward lore; knows every protection circle, half of the power circles and none of the summoning circles. Saving throw vs his magic is 14 or higher.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Scepter of Bedevilment: greatest rune weapon, a black rod like a mace, crowned with two dragon heads and small wings; I.Q. 19, telepathic link, indestructible, reddish grey, aberrant (1D4x10 damage per melee to a good being holding it); 2D4x10 M.D.; animated, flies and fights on its own with three attacks per melee, +4 strike and parry, +2 initiative; returns by teleport when summoned. Magic bow: fires any arrow three times a longbow''s range, 1920 ft (585 m); usually carries a dozen lightning arrows, six Scathach alder and six Scathach oak arrows plus tech explosive and gas arrows. Glitter Boy Boom Gun (standard damage and range). Pair of forearm mini-missile launcher bands, four mini-missiles each, mixed types. Mini-missile cannon: fires volleys of 2, 4, 6, 8 or 10, auto-reloads, 30-missile payload, needs supernatural P.S. 50+. Armor: golden plate, 3000 M.D.C. Shuns bionics and cybernetics but likes technology.', '2D4x10 million credits in precious metals and gems, plus an arsenal of ancient and modern weapons and some magic and tech items.', 'An honorable warrior by his own code: generous and even friendly toward brave and noble foes, contemptuous and cruel to cowards and backstabbers. Loves contests and likes humans for their courage.', 'Serves Set as war advisor, commander and assassin but largely goes his own way; friends with Styphathal of Atlantis, Zandragal of the Dragon Wright Pantheon and other ancient dragons; knows the Joker of Palladium, the Sunaj, Atlantean undead slayers and kittani; 10,000 loyal ramen; uses gremlins, gallu bulls, tautons and worms of Taut; favors raksasha, baal-rog and sowki; worshipped by humans and D-bee warriors as well as Phoenix Empire non-humans.', 'Many across the Megaverse, including Gods of Light and Darkness outside the Nile gods; dislikes Pharaoh Rama-Set; a natural foe of the Four Horsemen, whom he may fight once two or more have joined; considering secretly helping the humans against the Gargoyle Empire.', 'The lion-headed warrior god of the Pantheon of Taut, a master strategist and weapon master and patron of mercenaries, assassins and diabolists. He has only just returned to Earth after more than 5000 years away and often travels with 3D4 ramen.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.45-46');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'ammit-africa', 'Ammit', 'Ammiti-nupi', 'The Beast', 'rifts', 'Deity', '10th level Fighter and 4th level Necromancer', 10, 'Miscreant', NULL, '28 feet (8.5 m) long, 10 feet (3 m) tall', NULL, '{"IQ":12,"ME":24,"MA":7,"PS":40,"PP":22,"PE":24,"PB":3,"Spd":66}', NULL, NULL, 5000, 1000, 750, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":7,"parry":8,"dodge":8,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'Six hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 19-20, triple damage from behind. +5 save vs psionics, +5 save vs all magic, +5 save vs poison and drugs, +9 save vs horror factor. Supernatural P.S.; Spd 66 is 45 mph. Holy weapons, silver weapons (which do M.D. to him), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do double damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":88},{"name":"Biology","pct":88},{"name":"Climbing","pct":88},{"name":"Swimming","pct":88},{"name":"Fishing","pct":88},{"name":"Hunting","pct":88},{"name":"Track Humanoids","pct":88},{"name":"Track Animals","pct":88},{"name":"Skin and Prepare Animal Hides","pct":88},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":88},{"name":"Cook","pct":88},{"name":"Dance","pct":88},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":88},{"name":"Detect Concealment","pct":88},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":88},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":88},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":88}]', NULL, 'Nightvision 1000 ft (305 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 91%, dimensional teleport 78%, metamorphosis into any shape, heat, cold and fire do half damage, summons/commands 1D4 werebeasts, bio-regenerates 3D6x10 M.D.C./minute (new limb overnight).', 'All necromancy spells and abilities at 4th level.', 'I.S.P. 750 at 10th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: all level 1-2 powers. Rifts: physical powers plus telepathy and electrokinesis.', NULL, NULL, 'None; no special magic weapons and no armor. Fights only with his body, magic and psionics and avoids technology.', '1D6 million credits in precious metals and gems, plus some magic and tech items.', 'A devouring predator wholly obedient to Anubis; badly underestimates humans and D-bees.', 'Loyal servant of Anubis and respects his alliances; favors werebeasts and fenry wolves; keeps company with fiends and archfiends.', 'Anubis''s enemies.', 'A monstrous god with a crocodile''s head, a lion''s forequarters and a hippo''s hindquarters who guards Anubis, kills and eats his foes and devours the dead. Patron of assassins and predators and a symbol of despair and lycanthropy.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.46-47');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'bes-africa', 'Bes', 'Bes-shuvin', 'The Depraved', 'rifts', 'Deity', '9th level Mystic, 8th level Stone Master', 9, 'Diabolic', NULL, '5 feet (1.5 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":17,"ME":24,"MA":24,"PS":41,"PP":24,"PE":27,"PB":6,"Spd":33}', NULL, NULL, 6000, 1500, 950, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":6,"strike":7,"parry":8,"dodge":8,"roll":2,"pull":4}', 'Six hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. +7 strike is hand to hand. Critical strike on a natural 18-20. +5 save vs psionics, +5 save vs all magic, +5 save vs poison and drugs, +7 save vs horror factor; 80% to evoke intimidation or trust. Supernatural P.S.; Spd 33 is 22.5 mph. Insanities: psychotic murderer, sadist, obsessed with cannibalism and with danger (needless risks), phobia of Osiris and anyone wielding his body parts. Holy weapons, silver weapons (which do M.D. to him), Millennium Tree wood and some rune weapons do double damage. Magic cold hurts him double as well.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":89},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":89},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":89},{"name":"Climbing","pct":89},{"name":"Swimming","pct":89},{"name":"SCUBA","pct":89},{"name":"Palming","pct":89},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":89},{"name":"Pick Pockets","pct":89},{"name":"Dance","pct":89},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Guitar","pct":89},{"name":"Play Musical Instrument: Flute","pct":89},{"name":"Pilot Hover Vehicles","pct":89},{"name":"Pilot Boats","pct":89},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":89},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":60},{"name":"Radio: Scrambler","pct":60},{"name":"TV/Video","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Programming","pct":60},{"name":"Forgery","pct":60},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":60},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":60},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese","pct":60},{"name":"Literacy: Euro","pct":60}]', NULL, 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees and turns invisible at will, knows all languages, teleport 93%, dimensional teleport 77%, never tires, can turn into a toad, snake or rat, bio-regenerates 4D6x100 points/minute (new limb overnight). Priestly powers: exorcism 40%, turn dead 69% (3D6x10 dead), remove magic curse 44%, resurrection 32%, unlimited healing touch 2D6 S.D.C./hit points.', 'All stone magic plus agony, befuddle, blinding flash, call lightning, carpet of adhesion, chameleon, domination, energy disruption, fear, fuel flame, globe of daylight, life drain, luck curse, magic net, mask of deceit, mute, mystic alarm, negate magic and summon and control canine. Ley line magic at 9th level, stone magic at 4th. Saving throw vs his spells is 14 or higher.', 'I.S.P. 950 at 9th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: all level 1-3 powers. Rifts: all physical powers plus mind bond, mind wipe and mentally possess others.', NULL, NULL, 'Mee and Fea: twin silver greatest rune daggers with bat wings and strong, unruly personalities; indestructible, silver/grey, diabolic (1D4x10 damage per melee to a good being holding one), telepathically linked to Bes; animated, return when thrown, fly and fight alone with three attacks per melee, +4 strike and parry, +2 initiative. Mee (I.Q. 10), a sadist who hates women and children and is used for torture: 6D6 S.D.C. or M.D. Fea (I.Q. 13), paranoid schizophrenic and pyromaniac: 1D6x10 M.D. and at will, one power per two melees, fire ball, wall of flame, circle of flame or spontaneous combustion. Also favors neuro-maces, vibro-blades, laser scalpels and energy rifles; seldom wears armor. Collects torture and spy technology; shuns bionics and cybernetics.', '1D4x10 million credits in precious metals and gems, a small arsenal of old and new weapons, and some magic and tech items.', 'A mad, sadistic murderer and cannibal who takes pointless risks and revels in torture; fascinated by gadgets that cause pain or spy on people.', 'Set, Amon and the Gods of Darkness; Apepi counts him a friend; knows Lord Splynncryth and Styphathal of Atlantis; honorary Sunaj assassin. Favors manticores, chimeras, spectres, boogie-men and loogaroo; associates with werebeasts, evil dwarves, ancient evil sphinxes and dragons.', 'The forces of good; terrified of Osiris.', 'Once a merry god of love and feasting who fought beside Ra, Bes fell to savagery and madness and was recruited by Set. He appears as a golden-skinned, bearded dwarf in Egyptian dress with a feathered headdress.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.47-48');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'ra-africa', 'Ra', 'Ra Annu', 'Lord of Light, the Sun God', 'rifts', 'Deity (Nile God, Pantheon of Ra)', '20th level air and fire warlock; 12th level stone master and spell caster', 20, 'Scrupulous', NULL, '40 feet (12.2 m); can shrink to 12 feet in six-foot steps', NULL, '{"IQ":23,"ME":28,"MA":27,"PS":38,"PP":22,"PE":28,"PB":27,"Spd":88}', NULL, NULL, 14000, 6000, 2000, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":4,"strike":7,"parry":10,"dodge":10,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Seven hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 18-20. +7 save vs psionic attack, +7 save vs all magic, +8 save vs poison and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor. 92% intimidation or trust, 83% charm or impress. Supernatural P.S. and attributes; speed 88 is about 60 mph (96 km). Opponents need a 15 or better to save against his magic. Vulnerable: rune magic, bio-wizard weapons and silver weapons (silver does M.D. to him) all do double damage. Wears gold plate armor of 1000 M.D.C. (not included in the M.D.C. above).', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy","pct":98},{"name":"Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Disguise","pct":98},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":65},{"name":"Laser","pct":65},{"name":"Basic Electronics","pct":65},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":65},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":65}]', 'Disguise is by way of metamorphosis. Also W.P. Blunt and W.P. Sword (no percentage printed).', 'Hawk-sharp sight out to two miles (3.2 km), nightvision 200 feet (61 m), sees the invisible, turns invisible at will with no time limit, knows every language, teleport 96%, dimensional teleport 94%, metamorphosis into any shape at will (including a fully human look), flies at 90 mph (148 km), and takes no harm from heat, cold or fire. Resizes between 12 and 40 feet tall in six-foot (1.8 m) increments. Priestly powers: exorcism 80%, turn dead 97% (2D6x100 dead at once), healing touch 4D6 S.D.C./hit points twice per melee, bio-regeneration 1D4x100 M.D.C. per minute and a lost limb regrown overnight. Resurrection touch, once per subject: 1-80% if dead no more than a month (back with full S.D.C. and 3D6 hit points, and the fatal harm is healed but not lost limbs or scars), 1-40% if dead a month to a year, 3% beyond a year. None of these cost P.P.E.', 'Spell magic levels 1-8; air and fire elemental (warlock) magic levels 1-8; every stone magic spell; every symbol, ward, curse, and protection or summoning circle; and additionally close rift, remove curse, teleport: superior, dimensional portal and stone to flesh. Spell, stone and diabolist magic at 12th level; air and fire elemental magic at 20th level warlock. Save needs a 15 or better.', 'I.S.P. 2000; proficiency equal to 20th level. Palladium RPG: every ability of levels 1-5. Rifts: every sensitive and physical power, with pyrokinesis, electrokinesis, mind block auto-defense and psi-sword added.', NULL, NULL, 'Scepter of the Greyhound: gold, greyhound-headed greatest rune scepter (blunt), I.Q. 16, telepathic link to Ra, indestructible, scrupulous; evil or anarchist beings touching it take 1D6x10 per melee held. Casts dispel magic barrier, call lightning, calm storms, wind rush, extinguish fires and heal burns (full restoration, no scars), each six times per 24 hours at 15th level. Strikes for 2D4x10 M.D., 2D4x100 to vampire intelligences and double damage against ghouls, zombies, animated dead and vampires. Can blaze with sunlight over a 3000 foot (914 m) radius that affects vampires and vampire intelligences as full noon sun. Also a Millennium Tree staff of life with 14 buds (Rifts England p.20) and 1D6x10 other magic items at GM discretion. Gold plate armor, 1000 M.D.C. Occasionally plasma or laser rifles while disguised as a human.', '2D4 billion credits in precious metals and jewels, plus assorted magic and technological items.', 'Stern and single-minded; sees the world as a plain contest of light against darkness in which evil must be destroyed and fallen champions avenged. Little interest in politics. Tolerates technology as another form of power and lets followers use it, but uses no bionics himself and detests bio-wizardry.', 'Isis and most of the Pantheon of Ra, other good beings and champions of light; loyal ramen and fire and air elementals; drawn to spirits of light, elementals, ancient dragons and creatures of magic.', 'Apepi (his arch-foe), Set, Anubis, the jinn and vampire intelligences; all dark gods, demon lords, alien intelligences and Splugorth (including Lord Splynncryth), though he mostly fights those who oppose him directly.', 'The oldest and most elemental of the Nile gods, embodiment of the sun, life and fertility, shown as a giant golden-skinned humanoid with a hawk''s head, a sun disk crown and the Scepter of the Greyhound. He judges Earth''s balance of good and evil adequate for now, fights elsewhere in the Megaverse, and has left a few hundred ramen watching Africa, the Mediterranean and old Egypt.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.49-52');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'thoth-africa', 'Thoth', 'Thoth (originally Xy)', 'Lord of Wisdom', 'rifts', 'Deity (Nile God, Pantheon of Ra); secretly a transformed Old One', 'Ley line walker, rune master and diabolist at 30th level; stone master at 20th; techno-wizard at 10th; bio-wizard at 8th; alchemist at roughly 12th', 30, 'Unprincipled', NULL, '20 feet (6 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":30,"ME":23,"MA":27,"PS":39,"PP":22,"PE":27,"PB":25,"Spd":88}', NULL, NULL, 40000, 6000, 2000, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":4,"strike":6,"parry":8,"dodge":8,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'M.D.C.: the book gives 14,470, which is what Thoth believes he has; his true figure is 40,000 (an alien intelligence''s), and 40000 is stored. Five hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 19 or 20. +5 save vs psionic attack, +7 save vs all magic, +7 save vs poison and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor. 94% intimidation or trust, 75% charm or impress. Supernatural P.S. and attributes; speed 88 is about 60 mph (96 km). Opponents need a 17 or better to save against his spell magic. Vulnerable: rune magic, bio-wizard weapons and silver weapons (silver does M.D. to him) all do double damage. Despite the M.D.C. he has none of an alien intelligence''s other powers.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"All Science skills","pct":98},{"name":"Electrical skills","pct":98},{"name":"Mechanical skills","pct":98},{"name":"Technical skills","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy (all major languages)","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot skills","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":76},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":76},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":76},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":76},{"name":"Disguise","pct":76},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":76},{"name":"Medical Doctor in Cybernetics","pct":76},{"name":"Pathology","pct":76},{"name":"Forensics","pct":76},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":76},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":76},{"name":"Cook","pct":76},{"name":"Demolitions","pct":76},{"name":"Demolitions Disposal","pct":76},{"name":"Computer Hacking","pct":76},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":76}]', 'The 98% entries are whole skill categories as printed. Disguise is by metamorphosis. Weapon proficiencies (no percentage printed): Blunt, Sword, Energy Pistol, Energy Rifle.', 'Sharp senses, nightvision 200 feet (61 m), sees the invisible, turns invisible at will with no time limit, knows every language, teleport 99%, dimensional teleport 96%, metamorphosis into any shape at will. Priestly powers: exorcism 90%, remove curse 90%, turn dead 90% (1D6x100 dead at once), healing touch 2D6 S.D.C./hit points twice per melee, bio-regeneration 1D4x100 M.D.C. per minute and a lost limb regrown overnight. None cost P.P.E. Absent-minded: a side effect of the circle that remade him erased almost all memory of his life as the Old One Xy and still costs him small memories; only dream fragments surface.', 'All symbols, circles and wards, all spell magic levels 1-15 including every spell of legend, and stone magic; no elemental magic and no necromancy. Save needs a 17 or better. Credited with inventing rune magic, the runic alphabet, diabolism, wards and pyramid magic, and forged many of the Nile gods'' greatest rune weapons.', 'I.S.P. 2000 at 15th level proficiency. Palladium RPG: every ability of levels 1-9. Rifts: every sensitive and super power.', NULL, NULL, 'Rod of Thoth: plain silver-gray rune staff wound with two silver serpents with ruby eyes; I.Q. 18, telepathic link to Thoth, indestructible, scrupulous; evil or anarchist beings touching it take 1D6x10 per melee held. Struck on the ground, up to six times a day at 10th level: earthquake (2D6x100 M.D. against structures, buildings and vehicles across 1000 ft/305 m), call lightning (2D6x10 M.D.), mystic portal, teleport: superior, id barrier, and an impenetrable wall of force 2000 ft (610 m) long by 100 ft (30.5 m) high with 5000 M.D.C.. Strikes for 2D4x10 M.D., double damage to vampires, vampire intelligences, zombies, ghouls and animated dead. Its two serpents come alive: three attacks each per melee, bite 2D6 M.D. or magic fire breath 4D6 M.D. (100 ft/30.5 m), +3 initiative, strike, parry and dodge; the staff itself can levitate and drift at Spd 12. 100 techno-wizard modified Triax Dyna-bots: magic powered with unlimited energy on Earth, crystal eyes; 20% carry magic flaming swords (4D6 M.D.), 20% are impervious to energy, 10% can turn invisible, 10% fly as the eagle; on ley lines and nexus points each gains a 200 M.D.C. energy field and doubled weapon range; his twelve Zembahk can ride them like power armor. Also nearly any techno-wizard device, herb, potion, magic or bio-wizard component, dozens of wands, staves, cauldrons, manacles, Millennium Tree items and amulets, a small zoo and artifacts of many civilizations; 65% likely to have any TW item from Rifts Ultimate Edition or the Vampires Sourcebook. Never wears armor.', '2D4 billion credits in precious metals and jewels, and four times that in magic items and components.', 'Curious, secretive and absent-minded; values knowledge for itself, admires cunning and quick wits, and often too absorbed in study or experiment to notice the Megaverse''s troubles. Hoards forbidden lore so no one, himself included, gains too much power. Takes readily to technology and experiments with bionics and bio-wizardry on willing (or persuaded) subjects.', 'Few true friends: Ra, Isis, Anhur and the raksasha Tygre-Slnn (8th level, anarchist); fond of the Splugorth. Countless acquaintances including the Nile gods, Pharaoh Rama-Set, Mrrlynn, Lord Splynncryth, Od, Narabium, Kym-nark-mar and the Joker of Palladium. Servants: 200 golems, 300 rune statues, 100 TW Dyna-bots, ramen, raksashas, a True Atlantean, a Splugorth High Lord, Kryanthal the thunder lizard (10th level techno-wizard), Lyphan the white sphinx, twelve Zembahk, two Shaydor spherians, twelve adarok flying mountains, 20 full conversion borgs and a za of anarchist alignment.', 'Amon the Hidden One and vampires (through his alliance with Ra and Isis); many resent him but few dare act.', 'The ibis-headed, robed god of wisdom, invention and magic, patron of the quick-witted and the light-fingered. Unknown to everyone, himself included, he is Xy, an Old One remade by his own experimental power circle after betrayal by Ya-Blik and Al-Vil; on Rifts Earth faint dreams of that past have begun to trouble him.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.52-54');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'isis-africa', 'Isis', 'Isis Sebhest', 'The All Mother & Warrior', 'rifts', 'Deity (Nile God, Pantheon of Ra)', '20th level ley line walker; 13th level stone master and diabolist', 20, 'Principled', NULL, '20 feet (6 m); alters size by metamorphosis', NULL, '{"IQ":24,"ME":25,"MA":27,"PS":37,"PP":27,"PE":27,"PB":27,"Spd":77}', NULL, NULL, 12000, 4000, 3000, NULL, 17, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":5,"strike":10,"parry":12,"dodge":12,"roll":6,"pull":6}', 'Horror/Awe Factor 17 in god form. M.D.C. 12,000, with crimson and gold plate armor adding 3000. Seven hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or ten long bow attacks, or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 18-20. +5 save vs psionic attack, +7 save vs all magic, +7 save vs poison and drugs, +10 save vs horror factor. 92% intimidation or trust, 83% charm or impress. Supernatural P.S. and attributes; speed 77 running (53 mph/85 km) or 220 flying (150 mph/241 km). Opponents need a 15 or better to save against her magic. Vulnerable: rune magic, bio-wizard weapons and silver weapons (silver does M.D. to her) all do double damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy","pct":98},{"name":"Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Disguise","pct":98},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"All W.P.s","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":65},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":65},{"name":"Prowl","pct":65},{"name":"Climb","pct":65},{"name":"Acrobatics","pct":65},{"name":"Palming","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":65}]', 'Disguise is by metamorphosis. All weapon proficiencies at 98% as printed.', 'Hawk-sharp sight out to two miles (3.2 km), nightvision 200 feet (61 m), sees the invisible, knows every language, teleport 94%, dimensional teleport 85%, metamorphosis at will into any humanoid, animal or bird (often a human woman), flight, half damage from heat, cold and fire, and can summon 1D4 Spirits of Light. Priestly powers: exorcism 81%, turn dead 81% (1D6x100 dead at once), remove curse 86%, healing touch 3D6 S.D.C./hit points twice per melee, bio-regeneration 1D4x100 M.D.C. per minute and a lost limb regrown overnight.', 'Every spell of levels 1-15, cast at 20th level; all stone magic and diabolism at 13th level. Save needs a 15 or better.', 'I.S.P. 3000; proficiency equal to 20th level. Palladium RPG: every ability of levels 1-6. Rifts: every healing and sensitive power, with psi-shield, psi-sword, group mind block, P.P.E. shield and mind block auto-defense added.', NULL, NULL, 'The Eternal Torch: black metal greatest rune torch whose flame never goes out and dispels magic darkness and fog within 30 feet (9 m); I.Q. 12, telepathic link to Isis, indestructible, scrupulous; evil or anarchist beings touching it are burned for 1D4x10. Casts circle of flame, globe of daylight, fuel flame, ignite fire, extinguish fires and heal burns, each six times per 24 hours at 10th level. As a flaming club 1D4x10 M.D., triple to animated skeletons, mummies and wood or cloth things; fires a magic-flame bolt up to three times per melee (one action each), 2000 ft (610 m), +1 strike, 1D6x10 M.D. Magic long bow: needs P.S. 24 to draw; silver moonbeam arrows 1D6x10 M.D., double to undead, devils, demons and evil supernatural beings, 4000 ft (1200 m), +3 strike; other arrows reach about 1200 ft (366 m); never fewer than a dozen moonbeam arrows. Sword of Isis (the Retributor): greatest rune bastard sword made by Thoth, black with a pale blue halo, I.Q. 15, telepathic link, indestructible, scrupulous (evil or anarchist touch 1D6x10); 1D6x10 M.D., double to vampires, mummies, zombies and animated dead. Its Light of Retribution blast, six times per 24 hours, deals 1D6x100 M.D. to evil supernatural beings and to creatures of magic (dragons, demons and the like) and leaves good or selfish beings untouched, +3 strike, no save. Crimson and gold plate armor, 3000 M.D.C.', '2D4 billion credits in precious metals and jewels, plus assorted magic and technological items.', 'Compassionate, merciful and honorable, yet a fierce warrior who cannot abide injustice. Finds technology a quaint toy next to magic but lets others use it and passes captured gear to deserving followers. Forever hunting the scattered remains of Osiris.', 'Most of her pantheon and good beings everywhere; great warriors, elementals, spirits of light, ancient dragons and creatures of magic. Her secret human guise is Katrina Sun, who has joined the Gathering of Heroes against the Four Horsemen.', 'Set, Anubis, Apepi, the gods who helped kill Osiris, the jinn and vampires; all Splugorth including Lord Splynncryth, though she fights only those who oppose her or her champions.', 'Highest mother-goddess of the Nile pantheon, a winged, silver-haired beauty with cow horns who carries a torch and a black bow, worshipped across the Megaverse under countless names. Officially too busy in other dimensions to heed Earth, she is in fact walking among its heroes in human disguise.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.54-55');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'horus-africa', 'Horus', 'Harmakhis Heru-Ur-Sebhest', 'Harmakhis the Great Sphinx', 'rifts', 'Great Sphinx (Nile God, Pantheon of Ra)', '12th level fire warlock; 7th level stone master and diabolist', 12, 'Scrupulous', NULL, 'Stands 19 feet (5.85 m), 40 feet (12 m) long; can shrink to about 6 feet tall and 12 feet long', NULL, '{"IQ":21,"ME":28,"MA":26,"PS":40,"PP":26,"PE":27,"PB":25,"Spd":88}', NULL, NULL, 5500, 2500, NULL, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":8,"parry":10,"dodge":10,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Great sphinxes have 6D6x100 M.D.C. plus 100 per level, to a maximum of 6000; M.D.C. is halved while in human form and returns on changing back. Horror/Awe Factor 16. Six hand to hand attacks per melee or two by spell. Critical strike on a natural 18-20. +7 save vs psionic attack, +6 save vs all magic, +6 save vs poison and drugs, +8 save vs horror factor. 88% intimidation or trust, 75% charm or impress. Supernatural P.S. and attributes; speed 88 running (60 mph/96 km) or 293 flying (200 mph/321 km). Opponents need a 14 or better to save against his magic. No real vulnerabilities beyond a tendency to be selfish, obsessive and to underestimate lesser beings. Great sphinx life span about 12,000 years.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy","pct":98},{"name":"Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Fishing","pct":98},{"name":"Herbology","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Sail and Rowboats","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Dragonese (speak and read)","pct":98},{"name":"Euro (speak and read)","pct":98},{"name":"Spanish (speak and read)","pct":98},{"name":"Ancient Egyptian (speak and read)","pct":98},{"name":"Gobblely (speak)","pct":98},{"name":"Faerie Speak (speak)","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":60},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":60}]', 'Weapon proficiencies in the 98% group: Sword, Targeting/Spear, Heavy Energy Weapons, Energy Weapons.', 'Hawk-sharp sight out to two miles (3.2 km), nightvision 600 feet (183 m), sees the invisible; at 80%: track by sight, walk tightrope, sense of balance and flying backflip; at 60%: prowl, climb and swim; leaps 100 feet (30.5 m) up or across, flight, half damage from heat and fire, bio-regeneration 1D6x10 M.D.C. per minute and a lost appendage, organ or eye regrown within a week. Can metamorphose at will and indefinitely into a human, a human-like humanoid or a hawk-headed humanoid (usually bronze or golden maned, green eyed and dark skinned), at half M.D.C.', 'Fire warlock spells of levels 1-8, cast at 12th level; all stone and diabolist magic at 7th level. Save needs a 14 or better.', 'None; great sphinxes have no psionics.', NULL, NULL, 'Spear of Horus: long dark grey rune spear, needs P.S. 24 to wield; I.Q. 11, telepathic link to Horus, indestructible, unprincipled alignment; evil beings touching it take 1D4x10. Casts the same six spells as the Eternal Torch (circle of flame, globe of daylight, fuel flame, ignite fire, extinguish fires, heal burns), each six times per 24 hours at 10th level. 1D6x10 M.D. stabbing, 2D6x10 M.D. thrown (2000 ft/610 m, +2 strike), vanishing and returning to the thrower''s hand after it hits. Drawing blood forces any shape changer or metamorphosed being back to natural form, no save. Also a modest arsenal of rail guns, lasers, explosives and particle beam weapons; can wear any human armor in humanoid form.', '2D4 million credits in precious metals and jewels, plus some magic and technological weapons.', 'Gentle and tender toward weaker beings such as humans, merciful even to hated foes on the battlefield, but sworn to avenge Osiris. Likes technology as a tool for good, favoring lasers, particle beams and rail guns, though he needs no bionics.', 'Devoted to Isis and loyal to Ra and every other member of his pantheon; works with ramen, spirits of light and any good creature championing a just cause. Distrusts ancient dragons and his fellow great sphinxes. His cousin is Lyphan the White Sphinx.', 'Set, Anubis and Apepi above all; vampires; all Splugorth including Lord Splynncryth, though he fights only those opposing him or his allies.', 'A great sphinx, one of a rare dragon-class breed of super-sphinx, with a lion''s body, eagle''s wings and a human face. Raised as the adopted son of Isis and Osiris rather than their true child, he stands as the pantheon''s champion of justice, hope and the dawn.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.56-57');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'bennu-africa', 'Bennu', 'Bennu Helio', 'The Phoenix', 'rifts', 'Deity (Phoenix; Nile God, Pantheon of Ra)', 'Diabolist (10th level) and mind mage (10th level)', 10, 'Unprincipled', NULL, '20 feet (6 m) as bird or humanoid; can shrink to 10 feet (3 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":17,"ME":20,"MA":20,"PS":30,"PP":26,"PE":30,"PB":28,"Spd":44}', NULL, NULL, 6000, 1800, 3000, NULL, 16, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":7,"parry":9,"dodge":9,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Alignment printed as Unprincipled (selfish good). Horror/Awe Factor 16. Six hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee. Critical strike on a natural 19 or 20. +3 save vs psionic attack, +8 save vs all magic, +8 save vs poisons, drugs and disease, +6 save vs horror factor. 60% intimidation or trust, 86% charm or impress. Supernatural P.S. and attributes; speed 44 running (30 mph/48 km) or 132 flying (90 mph/148 km). Opponents need a 14 or better to save against her magic. Vulnerable: plain iron weapons do M.D. to her and rune weapons do double damage. Drugs and poisons do half damage for half the duration.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy","pct":98},{"name":"Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Sing","pct":98},{"name":"Art","pct":60},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":60},{"name":"Swim","pct":60},{"name":"Climb","pct":60},{"name":"Pilot Sailboat","pct":60},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":60}]', NULL, 'Hawk-sharp sight out to three miles (4.8 km), nightvision 1200 feet (366 m), sees the invisible, impervious to fire and heat, breathes without air, teleport and dimensional teleport both 94%, turns into a female humanoid at will, flight, and can summon 1D4 Spirits of Light, 1D4 phoenixi, or fire or air elementals. Instant bio-regeneration and restoration: can regrow lost M.D.C., limbs and organs in seconds without limit, but after the first instant regeneration from major damage her maximum M.D.C. halves to 3000, and each later one halves it again (1500, 750 and so on); limbs and organs regrow without penalty. Otherwise recovers 100 M.D.C. per hour. Effectively immortal: even if destroyed utterly she is reborn whole within 2D4 weeks.', 'Every diabolist ward, circle and symbol, at 10th level. Save needs a 14 or better.', 'I.S.P. 3000; proficiency equal to 20th level. Palladium RPG: every ability of levels 1-10. Rifts: every physical and sensitive power, with super telekinesis, mind bond, mind bolt, hypnotic suggestion, empathic transmission, bio-manipulation, group mind block, P.P.E. shield and mind block auto-defense added.', NULL, NULL, 'None. She fights with her natural, psionic and magic powers and wears no armor; her hoard includes magic and high-tech gear, much of it beyond her ability to use.', 'Hoard of at least 2D4x100 million credits in gems and precious metals, plus 1D6x10 million in magic and technological items.', 'The most animal of the Nile gods: savage in battle, a born hunter, and ruled by self-preservation to the point of letting innocents die rather than risk herself. Dodges obligations that pay her nothing, yet at heart feels bound to help, so she prefers not to hear of trouble at all. Indifferent to most technology, curious about bionics, and hates bio-wizardry.', 'The phoenixi (who call her All-mother), Isis and the Gods of Light; spirits of light and elementals, who treat her like a stepsister.', 'Set and Anubis above all, for the phoenixi slaughtered in their experiments (Set once killed 1100 in a rage); most evil supernatural beings. She will stay out of the fight against the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse.', 'Goddess of death, rebirth and the turning of day and season, taking the form of a huge bird of prey or a lovely woman in a gown of feathers. She keeps her distance from the affairs of gods and mortals unless there is something in it for her, revenge included.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.57-58');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'apis-africa', 'Apis', 'Apis', 'The Sacred Cow', 'rifts', 'Deity (Nile God, Pantheon of Ra)', '15th level earth warlock and psionic', 15, 'Scrupulous', NULL, '18 feet (5.5 m); alters size by metamorphosis', NULL, '{"IQ":15,"ME":25,"MA":20,"PS":36,"PP":21,"PE":25,"PB":18,"Spd":77}', NULL, NULL, 6500, 1400, 900, NULL, 15, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":6,"parry":8,"dodge":8,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Horror/Awe Factor 15. Four hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by magic. Critical strike on a natural 19 or 20. +5 save vs psionic attack, +5 save vs all magic, +5 save vs poison and drugs, +5 save vs horror factor. 60% intimidation or trust, 50% charm or impress. Supernatural P.S. and attributes; speed 77 running (53 mph/85 km). Opponents need a 15 or better to save against her magic. Vulnerable: rune magic and magic fire do double damage.', '[{"name":"Basic Math","pct":98},{"name":"Astronomy","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"All Wilderness skills","pct":98},{"name":"Herbology","pct":98},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Identify Plants & Fruits","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Sail and Rowboats","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98}]', 'Can use nearly any ancient weapon, preferring blunt ones (no W.P. percentage printed).', 'Keen vision, nightvision 200 feet (61 m), sees the invisible, knows every language, teleport 90% and dimensional teleport 50%, takes the shape of any hoofed animal at will, and can summon 1D4 Ariel Spirits of Light. Communicates by empathy and telepathy. Priestly powers: exorcism 81%, turn dead 44% (1D6x10 dead at once), remove curse 74%, healing touch 4D6 S.D.C./hit points twice per melee, bio-regeneration 1D4x100 M.D.C. per minute and a lost limb regrown within 48 hours.', 'Earth warlock spells of levels 1-8, cast at 15th level. Save needs a 15 or better.', 'I.S.P. 900; proficiency equal to 20th level. Palladium RPG: every level 1 and 2 ability. Rifts: every sensitive and healing power, with mind block auto-defense and group mind block added.', NULL, NULL, 'A Millennium Tree wand of dowsing and a Staff of Earth (Rifts England p.19-20), and nearly any magic herb, tea or potion from Rifts England short of the rare ones. No armor; never uses technology.', '1D4 million credits in precious metals and jewels; she has little use for wealth.', 'Deeply empathic, motherly and compassionate, above all toward children, the old and the sick. Believes technology harms nature and gently argues others out of it, meeting its users with sorrow rather than anger.', 'Druids, earth warlocks and the Ariel spirits; most of her pantheon, though her anti-technology views cause friction. Minions: earth elementals, the Ariel, druids, and sometimes the gallu bull, ramen and phoenixi.', 'Set, Anubis, Apepi and the jinn, and anything unnatural or destructive; all Splugorth including Lord Splynncryth, though she fights only those who oppose her or her champions.', 'Goddess of fertility, growth and restoration who watches over healers, druids and priests, appearing as a big woman with a cow''s head, robed in white. She is currently occupied in another dimension and knows nothing of what is unfolding on Earth.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.58-59');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'rama-set', 'Pharaoh Rama-Set', 'Tor Li', 'Pharaoh of the Phoenix Empire', 'rifts', 'Chiang-Ku Dragon', '12th level Tattoo Master and 7th level Necromancer', 12, 'Diabolic', NULL, '6 ft 4 in (1.93 m) in human form', NULL, '{"IQ":25,"ME":21,"MA":26,"PS":26,"PP":20,"PE":21,"PB":10,"Spd":20}', NULL, NULL, 1300, 900, 70, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"strike":5,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"damage":6,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'M.D.C. is 1300 in human form and 2300 in his true dragon form; attributes are supernatural. Also known as Lo Li. Five attacks per melee by hand to hand, tattoo magic or psionics. Critical strike on unmodified 18-20, paired weapons. +1 save vs psionics, +3 save vs spell and illusionary magic, +1 save vs circle magic, +4 save vs horror factor. The Tattoos of Masters add +1 save vs all magic, +2 save vs horror factor, +2 to P.E., and double-speed P.P.E. recovery.', '[{"name":"Disguise","pct":96},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":98},{"name":"Forgery","pct":91},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":87},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Faerie","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98}]', 'Basic math at 98%. R.C.C. skills include an I.Q. bonus of +11%. W.P. knife, sword, blunt, energy pistol and energy rifle. Hand to hand: expert.', 'Immune to poison, toxins, drugs and gases; nightvision to 90 ft (27.4 m); sees the invisible; fire and cold do half damage; bio-regenerates 1D6x5 M.D. every five minutes. Chiang-ku metamorphosis: can take any living animal shape from cat-sized up to his own size, or become mist, and hold it indefinitely (only coma or death reverts him); can impersonate a specific person or animal at 10% +5% per level after the first.', 'Understands magic fully and knows all tattoo magic and of making the Elixir of Power and Deceit; also a 7th level necromancer. Marks of Heritage plus power tattoos: chain encircling a skull (+3 save vs psionics), eye of knowledge (all languages), eye of mystic knowledge (reads magic symbols and runes), heart with large wings (flight at 130 mph/208 km), phoenix rising from flames (super healing and resurrection), skull with bat wings (animate dead). Animal tattoos: vulture, lion, elephant (rideable). Monster tattoos: Tri-Fang Worm of Taut, Mokele-mbembe/Erythrusuchus. Simple weapon tattoos: silver knife (1D4 S.D.C.), wooden cross.', 'Major psionic: alter aura, death trance, ectoplasm, levitation, telekinesis, summon inner strength, mind block. I.S.P. 70.', NULL, NULL, 'Carries nothing special and leans on his magic; no body armor. Tattoo magic weapons: flaming broadsword wrapped by a coiled snake (2D6 M.D., 6D6 M.D. against dragons and M.D. serpents or reptiles) and flaming knife wrapped by a coiled snake (1D6 M.D., 3D6 M.D. to dragons). Rides a sand skimmer.', 'A personal fortune of 100 million credits; as Pharaoh he can draw on ten billion credits and the whole Empire''s resources.', 'Insane and growing madder each year; worships chaos as the road to enlightenment and wants to set the whole Megaverse burning. A cunning strategist, a superb liar and a master of disguise.', 'Set and the Pantheon of Taut (whose favored agent he is), Anubis, Lord Splynncryth, Sunaj assassins, Blood Druids, many death cults and priests of the dark gods, demons, and the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse, who will spare him. Advisors include the raksasha Hass Uyban and the witch Mbau Ngbuto.', 'Lo Fung, his one-time friend, and the Gathering of Heroes; he has put bounties on rebels and knights (100,000 credits), Fang-Lo (500,000) and Abkii the Defiant (one million).', 'A Chiang-Ku dragon once called Lo Li who lived disguised among humans for millennia, was driven mad by the Great Cataclysm, and now rules the Phoenix Empire as a human-seeming Pharaoh. He summoned the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse to Earth, though they arrived scattered across Africa rather than at the Giza rift.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.141-144');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'katrina-sun', 'Katrina Sun', 'Isis', 'Line Walker and Worshipper of the Gods of Light', 'rifts', 'Deity (disguised as a human)', '15th level Ley Line Walker (as she believes)', 15, 'Principled good', NULL, '6 ft (1.8 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":24,"ME":25,"MA":27,"PS":37,"PP":27,"PE":27,"PB":27,"Spd":38}', NULL, NULL, 6000, 2000, 1500, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":5,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'All figures already carry the anti-god microbe penalties (M.D.C., speed, combat and save bonuses halved; skills -20%). Attributes are supernatural. Spd 38 is about 28 mph (45 km) running; she has forgotten she can fly. She thinks of herself as having 63 H.P. and 30 S.D.C. Horror/Awe Factor does not apply in human form. Four hand to hand actions, five longbow attacks, or two spell attacks per melee. Critical strike on natural 19-20. +2 save vs psionics, +3 save vs all magic, +3 save vs poison and drugs, +5 save vs horror factor; 92% intimidation or trust, 83% charm or impress. May be -2 initiative when distracted by her unexplained powers.', '[{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":78},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":45},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":45},{"name":"Prowl","pct":45},{"name":"Climbing","pct":45},{"name":"Acrobatics","pct":45},{"name":"Palming","pct":45},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":45}]', 'Basic and advanced math, astronomy, navigation, land navigation, wilderness survival, intelligence, disguise via metamorphosis, holistic medicine, identify plants and fruits, preserve food and cooking are grouped with horsemanship at 78%; all W.P.s. Microbe penalties included.', 'Forgotten, but may surface in a crisis: hawk-keen sight to two miles (3.2 km), nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees the invisible, knows all languages, teleport 94%, dimensional teleport 85%, metamorphosis into any humanoid, animal or bird, flight, half damage from heat, cold and fire, and can summon 1D4 Spirits of Light. Priestly powers: exorcism 81%, turn dead 81% (1D6x100 at a time), remove curse 86%, healing touch (3D6 S.D.C. or hit points, twice per melee), bio-regeneration of 1D4x100 M.D.C. per minute and regrows a limb overnight. Vulnerable to rune magic, bio-wizard weapons and devices, and silver, which all do double damage. Tires after hard exertion but has twice human endurance and heals three times as fast.', 'Remembers only spell magic, levels 1-12 at 15th level proficiency; save is 15 or higher. Cannot use diabolism or stone magic, though she instinctively recognizes wards, symbols, circles, magic runes and the dangers of stone pyramids.', 'Does not remember having any. I.S.P. 1500 at 15th level: all healing and sensitive powers plus psi-sword, psi-shield, P.P.E. shield, group mind block and mind block auto-defense. Uses mind block auto-defense and P.P.E. shield unconsciously; telekinesis, telekinetic force field, group mind block or psi-sword may flare up in life-threatening moments.', NULL, NULL, 'A magic longbow with a dozen moonbeam arrows plus mixed high-tech and conventional arrows; a CS plasma rifle and a Wilk''s laser pistol. Human crusader armor, 70 M.D.C. Rides a trained pegasus (120 M.D.C., runs at Spd 22, flies at 132 or about 90 mph/148 km, four attacks per melee). Unfamiliar with even simple machines.', '100,000 credits and 17,000 in gems.', 'Sincere and heroic but frightened and confused by powers and knowledge she cannot explain; apologizes for them, blames an unseen ally, and may flee to be alone after a strange episode.', 'The Gathering of Heroes; Sir Winslow Thorpe counts her among his allies. Anyone who befriends her as Katrina earns the goddess lasting gratitude once her memory returns.', 'Set, who infected her with the microbe and may send forces to torment her and her companions.', 'The goddess Isis, disguised as a human, whose memory Set wiped with an experimental Splugorth-made bio-wizard microbe that attacks gods; she now believes she is a human ley line walker. The illness will not kill her, and the GM decides when, if ever, she recovers her memory and full power.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.145-147');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'victor-lazlo', 'Victor Lazlo', 'Victor Charles Lazlo', 'Professor of Parapsychology', 'rifts', 'Human', '12th level Parapsychologist (roughly a Rogue Scholar)', 12, 'Scrupulous', 'about 55 (should be 63; displaced in time)', '5 ft 11 in (1.79 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":14,"ME":19,"MA":19,"PS":17,"PP":11,"PE":14,"PB":10,"Spd":11}', 71, 47, NULL, 19, 123, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":1,"parry":4,"dodge":5,"roll":4,"pull":4,"damage":2}', 'Hand to hand: basic at 11th level proficiency. Critical strike on unmodified 19-20, kick 1D6 S.D.C., judo body throw (1D6, victim loses initiative and one attack). +3 save vs psionics, +3 save vs horror factor, +2 save vs magic and poison, +3 save vs mind-altering drugs and potions, +2 save vs possession, +8% save vs coma/death. Cybernetic bonuses included. Wears Triax environmental body armor (80 M.D.C.).', '[{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":90},{"name":"Lore: Geomancy/Ley Lines","pct":90},{"name":"Language: American","pct":98},{"name":"Language: French","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Recognize Magic Wards and Circles","pct":86},{"name":"Perform Ritual Magic from Notes","pct":94},{"name":"Recognize Psychic Powers","pct":98},{"name":"Recognize Mind Control","pct":98},{"name":"Recognize Psionic and Techno-Wizard Devices","pct":66},{"name":"Recognize Rune Weapons","pct":98}]', 'Basic and advanced math, computer operation, biology, psychology, anthropology, parapsychology, research, photography, radio basic and scramblers; literate in American, French and Spanish. Speaks Gobblely and Euro, reads sensory equipment, first aid, swimming, climbing, running, wrestling, horsemanship, pilot automobile and pilot power armor (Ulti-Max, Hopper), all about 80%. W.P. knife, automatic pistol and energy rifle at 5th level. Can gauge a psychic''s degree of power and type at 66%.', 'A natural leader: intelligent, curious, analytical, strong-willed and resourceful.', 'Not a spell caster, but understands how magic, spells and ley lines work; reads magic runes and symbols and can read scrolls.', 'A latent psychic whose abilities are never available at will; they switch on by themselves under stress: sense magic, speed reading, mind block, impervious to cold, hunches and dream warnings (clairvoyance), and rarely see the invisible. Uses meditation. I.S.P. 123.', NULL, 'Gyro-compass, dosimeter/radiation detector, amplified hearing.', 'Silver cross, six wooden stakes and a mallet, survival knife (1D6), pocket knife (1 point), shotgun (7D6 S.D.C.), .45 automatic with 144 teflon armor-piercing rounds (6D6 S.D.C.) and 48 silver-coated rounds, Triax laser scalpel, Triax-30 ion pulse rifle (2D6 or 6D6 M.D., 2000 ft/610 m, a dozen 50-shot clips), TX-11 sniper rifle (3D6 M.D., 1600 ft/488 m). Pilots a stolen, fully armed X-1000 Ulti-Max (309 M.D.C. left on the main body) with a Triax T-21 Terrain Hopper as backup; Triax environmental body armor (80 M.D.C.). Also cameras, computers, a bio-scan, medical kit, nano-robot medical systems, translator and other field gear.', '1D6x10,000 credits on hand and about 500,000 at his base in Germany.', 'A scholar turned revolutionary who admires NGR technology but despises its human-supremacist treatment of D-bees and psychics; spends his time teaching and defending non-humans in the wastelands.', 'Many friends among D-bees, city rats and underground groups in and around the New German Republic; Lo Fung; likely to befriend Erin Tarn, Sir Thorpe and other heroes of the Gathering.', 'The New German Republic, which brands him an insane criminal; NGR/Triax troops will recognize him or his stolen Ulti-Max and attack.', 'The famous 20th Century parapsychologist who first described P.P.E., ley lines and supernatural predators, vanished atop an Ohio serpent mound in 1987, and emerged near the NGR in 94 P.A. After a stint in an asylum for claiming his own name, he now works with the underground helping non-humans.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.150-152');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'lo-fung', 'Lo Fung the Dragon', 'Lon Zin', 'The Dragon', 'rifts', 'Chiang-Ku Dragon', '15th level Tattoo Master', 15, 'Scrupulous', 'over 6,000 years on Earth', '5 ft (1.5 m) in human form', NULL, '{"IQ":26,"ME":22,"MA":26,"PS":24,"PP":19,"PE":18,"PB":15,"Spd":20}', NULL, NULL, 1100, 800, 100, NULL, 13, '{"attacks":5,"strike":5,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"damage":6,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'M.D.C. is 1100 in human form and 2100 in his true serpent form, before the +1125 M.D.C. of his Heart Encircled by Chains tattoo. Five attacks per melee by hand to hand, tattoo magic or psionics. Critical strike on unmodified 18-20, paired weapons. +4 save vs psionics, +5 save vs all magic, +6 save vs horror factor; recovers P.P.E. twice as fast.', '[{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":98},{"name":"Disguise","pct":98},{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Faerie","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Hovercraft","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Sailboat","pct":98},{"name":"Art","pct":98}]', 'All domestic skills and basic math also at 98%. R.C.C. skills include an I.Q. bonus of +7%. W.P. targeting, blunt/staff, sword, automatic pistol and energy rifle. Hand to hand: martial arts.', 'Immune to poison, toxins, drugs and gases; nightvision to 90 ft (27.4 m); sees the invisible; fire and cold do half damage; bio-regenerates 1D6x5 M.D.C. every five minutes. Chiang-ku metamorphosis (as Rama-Set); always appears as a human, usually an oriental monk.', 'Understands magic fully and knows all tattoo magic and of making the Elixir of Power and Deceit. Marks of Heritage plus power tattoos: Rose of Healing (healing touch), Phoenix Rising (super healing and resurrection), Heart Encircled by Chains (limited invulnerability, +1125 M.D.C.), Heart pierced by a wooden stake (protection from vampires), Skull Engulfed in Flames (fire power, fire bolt 1D4x15), Eye of Mystic Knowledge (reads magic symbols and runes). Animal tattoos: mongoose, tiger, horse (rideable). Monster tattoo: Yazhing Multipede. Simple weapon tattoos: bow and arrow (1D6 S.D.C.), wood staff (1D8 S.D.C.).', 'Major psionic: detect psionics, deaden pain, exorcism, induce sleep, psychic diagnosis, psychic purification, psychic surgery. I.S.P. 100.', NULL, NULL, 'An ordinary wood staff and a long bow with arrows; never wears armor. Tattoo magic weapons: flaming shield (indestructible, +2 to parry), flaming staff wrapped by a coiled snake (1D8 M.D., 3D8 M.D. against dragons and other M.D. serpents), flaming winged arrows (20 M.D. each, triple normal range).', 'Rarely more than 2D6x1000 credits, since he gives most of it to the poor.', 'Gentle, compassionate and devoted to humanity''s spiritual growth; blames himself for sparing Lo Li and has resolved to stop the Horsemen and then kill Rama-Set himself.', 'Victor Lazlo, the Nog Henge druids, Prrcyvel, his sect in the Orient, and heroes and kings across the Orient and parts of Europe; Sir Winslow Thorpe.', 'Pharaoh Rama-Set (Lo Li), his friend of millennia.', 'An ancient Chiang-Ku dragon living as a monk, a master arcanist and psychic who befriended Victor Lazlo in 1963 and later sustained the Lazlo Agency. He helped Lo Li survive the Cataclysm and learned only ten years ago that his old friend is the mad Pharaoh.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.152-154');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'fang-lo', 'Fang-Lo', 'Fang Lowana', NULL, 'rifts', 'Chiang-Ku Dragon (hatchling)', '5th level Tattoo Master', 5, 'Scrupulous', '497', NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":19,"ME":19,"MA":21,"PS":20,"PP":17,"PE":18,"PB":10,"Spd":15}', NULL, NULL, 200, 80, 110, NULL, 9, NULL, 'Quick stats only. M.D.C. is 200 in human form and 300 in her true serpent form.', NULL, 'Standard R.C.C. skills, 5th level.', 'Immune to poison, toxins, drugs and gases; nightvision to 90 ft (27.4 m); sees the invisible; fire and cold do half damage; bio-regenerates 1D6x5 M.D.C. every five minutes; chiang-ku metamorphosis.', 'Understands magic fully and knows all tattoo magic and of making the Elixir of Power and Deceit.', 'Major psionic: clairvoyance, sixth sense, telepathy, empathy, object read, presence sense, see aura, sense evil. I.S.P. 110.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Driven by troubling prophetic visions to stop four demon lords before they join forces.', 'Seeking Abkii the Defiant and other champions.', 'Pharaoh Rama-Set, who has put a 500,000 credit bounty on her head.', 'A young Chiang-Ku dragon whose visions showed four demon lords uniting at the New Phoenix with Rama-Set and the dark gods involved somehow. She has come to Africa to find Abkii and other heroes to stop them.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.154');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'abkii', 'Abkii the Defiant', 'Ob kee', 'The Defiant', 'rifts', 'Chiang-Ku Dragon (hatchling)', '6th level Tattoo Master and Warrior', 6, 'Unprincipled', '749', NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":17,"ME":20,"MA":20,"PS":22,"PP":21,"PE":20,"PB":8,"Spd":12}', NULL, NULL, 400, 60, 80, NULL, 9, NULL, 'Quick stats only. M.D.C. is 400 in human form and 500 in his true serpent form. Name pronounced Ob-Key.', NULL, 'Standard R.C.C. skills, 6th level, with hand to hand: martial arts, W.P. sword, targeting, blunt, energy pistol and energy rifle.', 'Immune to poison, toxins, drugs and gases; nightvision to 90 ft (27.4 m); sees the invisible; fire and cold do half damage; bio-regenerates 1D6x5 M.D.C. every five minutes; chiang-ku metamorphosis.', 'Understands magic fully and knows all tattoo magic and of making the Elixir of Power and Deceit.', 'Major psionic: alter aura, ectoplasm, impervious to fire and cold, resist fatigue, resist hunger, levitation, telekinesis. I.S.P. 80.', NULL, NULL, 'Sword of Atlantis (a rune weapon), Kittani plasma axe, a TW laser pulse rifle, and a talisman made by a pygmy shaman that lets him shadow meld twice a day. No numbers printed for these here.', NULL, 'A hard-drinking, brawling party animal who equally loves defending the weak, backing deserving underdogs and fighting against hopeless odds.', 'A wide circle of heroic warriors and mighty beings he has met on his travels, some of whom join his crusades; Fang-Lo is searching for him.', 'Pharaoh Rama-Set, who has offered one million credits for his head.', 'A roving Chiang-Ku dragon adventurer famous for revelry and reckless heroism. He went into the Phoenix Empire on some mission and has been missing ever since.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.154');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'sebek-africa', 'Sebek', 'Sebek Arimi', 'The Crocodile God', 'rifts', 'Deity', '15th level Con Artist and 10th level Line Walker', 15, 'Anarchist with leanings toward evil', NULL, '18 ft (5.5 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":20,"ME":19,"MA":19,"PS":40,"PP":18,"PE":28,"PB":10,"Spd":33}', NULL, NULL, 6470, 930, 120, NULL, 15, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":4,"strike":6,"parry":8,"dodge":8,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Attributes are supernatural. Spd 33 is about 22.5 mph (36 km), doubled when swimming. Per melee: seven hand to hand or psionic attacks, or two spell attacks. +3 to strike with energy weapons; critical strike on natural 19-20. +5 save vs psionics, +7 save vs all magic, +7 save vs poison and drugs, +6 save vs horror factor.', '[{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":98},{"name":"Forgery","pct":98},{"name":"Pick Pockets","pct":98},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":98},{"name":"Palming","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Hovercraft","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot Boats","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":60},{"name":"Radio: Scrambler","pct":60},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":60},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":60},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese","pct":60},{"name":"Literacy: Euro","pct":60},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98}]', 'Basic and advanced math at 98%. W.P. blunt, energy pistol and energy rifle. Swimming 98% is listed among his natural abilities.', 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees the invisible, knows all languages, turns into a crocodile or crocodillian, teleport 94%, dimensional teleport 83%, never tires, rarely sleeps, always alert; summons and controls 1D4x100 crocodiles and 2D4 crocodillians; bio-regenerates 1D4x100 per minute and regrows a limb within a week. Priestly powers: exorcism 50%, turn dead 50% (1D6x10 at a time), remove magic curse 34%, resurrection 10%, unlimited healing touch (2D6 S.D.C. or hit points). Holy weapons, silver, Millennium Tree wood, some rune weapons and magic fire do double damage.', 'All ley line walker spells levels 1-6, plus dispel magic barrier, negate magic, metamorphosis: human, life drain, minor curse, spoil, circles of protection, close rift, dimensional portal and teleport: superior, all at 10th level; save is 14 or higher.', 'Major psionic, I.S.P. 120: telepathy, mind block, and the super powers hypnotic suggestion, mind wipe and mentally possess others.', NULL, NULL, 'The Scepter of the Serpent (greatest rune weapon): a black mace-like rod with two crocodile heads, I.Q. 14 and telepathic, indestructible, anarchist (6D6 damage each melee to a good being holding it), soul drinking, 1D6x10 M.D. as a club, its heads breathe magic fire for 1D6x10 M.D. to 1000 ft (305 m), and it teleports back to him from anywhere, even other dimensions. A magic dagger (2D6 M.D., indestructible, never dulls, returns when thrown). A Glitter Boy Boom Gun (standard damage and range), carried because Anhur has one. Wears no armor; loves magic items and technology.', 'Can lay hands on 2D4 million credits in precious metals and jewels, plus an arsenal of ancient and modern weapons and some magic items and devices.', 'A selfish, petty, vindictive schemer who sides with whoever serves him, grows dangerous when bored, and may betray or abandon allies without warning.', 'The Gathering of Heroes for now, mainly to spite Set and the dark gods. Worshipped by crocodillians, some cults and a few African tribes; the crocodillians are his only truly loyal minions.', 'The Gods of Darkness, especially the Pantheon of Taut, who dislike him intensely; the Gods of Light avoid him.', 'A crocodile-headed god of mischief expelled from the Pantheon of Taut and unwelcome among the Gods of Light. He has joined the fight against the Apocalypse demons only to get even with Set.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.154-156');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stat_attacks (owner_kind, owner_slug, name, damage, is_mega_damage, range, note, sort) VALUES
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Restrained punch', '1D6x10 S.D.C.', 0, 'melee', NULL, 1),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Full strength punch', '6D6 M.D.', 1, 'melee', NULL, 2),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Power punch', '2D4x10 M.D.', 1, 'melee', NULL, 3),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Kick', '6D6 M.D.', 1, 'melee', NULL, 4),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Bite', '2D6 M.D.', 1, 'melee', NULL, 5),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Head butt', '2D6 M.D.', 1, 'melee', NULL, 6),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Staff of Death (strike)', '6D6 M.D.', 1, 'melee', 'double damage to vampires, undead, zombies, mummies and animated dead', 7),
  ('notable_npc', 'death-horseman', 'Staff of Death lightning bolt', '1D6x10 M.D.', 1, '2000 feet (610 m)', 'fired from the skull''s eyes; one blast per user attack', 8),
